WEBVTT

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:51.960
Damn ...

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.710
Where'd he go?

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:56.860
There!

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.790
Let's end this game here ...

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:28.880
Mr. Sneak-Thief.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.540
We should.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.090
It's growing too dark to continue playing hide-and-seek with you ...

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.930
Detective-kun.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.610
I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.410
While visiting an amusement park with my
childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran ...

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.120
I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.500
While caught up in watching the deal ...

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.130
I failed to notice his partner coming up behind me.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.130
Those men forced me to swallow poison ...

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.090
And when I came to ...

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.640
My body had shrunk.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.970
If those guys found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive ...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.890
They'd come after me again ...

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.350
And put those around me at risk.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.270
At Professor Agasa's suggestion, 
I decided to conceal my true identity.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.110
When Ran asked for my name, in that instant ...

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.440
I became Edogawa Conan.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.940
In order to obtain information on those guys ...

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.570
I went to live with Ran, whose father is a private detective.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.600
The culprit is ...

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.870
You!

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.830
This guy's name is Mouri Kogorou.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.670
Besides being Ran's father ...

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.540
He's now a detective so renowned even
crying babies have the respect to stay silent.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.510
The people call him "Sleeping Kogorou".

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.920
As for the reason behind that ...

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.400
I'm sure I don't have to explain that, right?

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.320
These two gadgets were both invented by Professor Agasa.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.780
Due to my shrinking, the professor invented
a number of unique gadgets for my use.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.740
Especially this Instant Soccer Ball Belt.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.330
When you push the button on the buckle ...

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.040
A self-inflating soccer ball comes out—a brilliant innovation.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.880
By the way ...

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.460
There are others that know my identity other than the professor.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.920
My mother and father ...

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.510
The high school Detective of the West, Hattori Heiji ...

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:06.930
And ...

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.350
A fellow elementary school classmate ...

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.430
Haibara Ai.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:16.230
She, along with her elder sister Miyano Akemi,
was a colleague of the men in black, but ...

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.110
Miyano Akemi was murdered by the organization.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.150
Upon hearing this, Haibara, in protest ...

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.820
Attempted to escape ...

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.740
By taking the same drug I had been forced to, and her body shrank.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.910
One more remains ...

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.210
Kaitou Kid.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.000
I've yet to put him behind bars.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.550
But, as a detective ...

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.970
I'll keep up the chase until I get him once and for all!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.850
Even though I've become smaller, my mind remains the same ...

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.220
The unbeaten great detective ...

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.720
There's always only one truth!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.170
10 Hours Earlier

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.210
I see.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.970
This is the advance notice you received from Kid?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:07.940
Yes.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.810
This morning, on the balcony of my apartment ...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.750
Maki Juri

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.750
Actress

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.750
This was placed, along with a large bouquet or roses.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.080
He's still as pretentious as ever.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.900
"Romeo, Juliet ..."

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.900
"Victor, Bravo ..."

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.830
"In the midst of where 26 letters fly about ...

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.790
Yaguchi Masayo

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.790
Manager

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.130
"I shall call upon you and gratefully accept the 'Jewel of Destiny'."

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.700
"Kaitou Kid."

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.160
Along with a playing card that's been split in half.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.920
Here you are.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:39.630
Thank you.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.300
Uhm ...

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.300
What's your opinion, Mouri-sensei?

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.140
Let's see here ...

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.850
This "Jewel of Destiny" would be—?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.320
It would be in reference to this.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.400
How pretty!

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.160
This is a star sapphire, then?

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.040
Yes.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.830
The three lines that intersect on its surface ...

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.870
Represent faith, hope, and fate.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.500
Thats is why it is known as the "Jewel of Destiny".

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.550
I see ...

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.050
It sure is magnificent!

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:31.300
It's perfect for Joséphine, whose love for
blue sapphires was no trifling matter ...

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.140
Which is why we're currently using it in the performance.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:34.430
Performance?

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:37.020
I've heard of it!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:43.110
It's a new theatre that opened in Shiodome called Sora, where
they're currently putting on a play called <i>Joséphine</i>, right?

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.460
Joséphine?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.440
She was Napoleon's first queen.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.820
She was also a well-known rose collector.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.680
I see.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.430
So that's why he sent the bouquet of roses.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.120
That's right, little boy.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.080
You seem to know a lot.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.790
Nah, he's only good for knowing trivial facts!

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.510
Romeo, Juliet ...

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.100
Victor, Bravo ...

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.480
Romeo, Juliet ...

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.480
Juri-san?

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:24.150
Yes?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:28.110
At the theatre where you're currently performing ...

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.700
Has there ever been a performance of <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>?

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.610
I didn't participate in the performance, but ...

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.200
It was Sora Theatre's maiden performance.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.080
Why do you ask?

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.040
I've figured it out.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:42.460
Really?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.170
In this advance notice Kid sent ...

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.880
We have three Ws and one H.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:51.090
In short ...

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:56.260
Who, when, where, and how ...

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.100
Are all communicated through its content.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.570
I see!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.440
Hey, hey ...

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.740
Can he pull this off?

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.060
Foremost is 'who'.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.690
This goes without saying—it's Kid.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.280
Then we have 'where'.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:14.240
That'd be where <i>Romeo and Juliet</i> was performed—the Sora stage.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.910
Next: 'when'.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:21.200
From the "Bravo" in the letter, we can take this
to mean when the audience is applauding.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.290
Lastly, we have 'how'.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.420
"Victor" refers to the conqueror.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:31.050
That is Napoleon, whom Kid intends to disguise as.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.840
Additionally, the playing card in the advance notice ...

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:37.800
It was split in half to make the "'V"' sign for victory.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:38.720
In other words ...

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:46.270
Kaitou Kid will appear on stage during your performance of
Joséphine, and, precisely when the audience applauds ...

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.150
He will, while disguised as Napoleon, attempt to steal the ring.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:53.320
Bravo!

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.150
Bravo, Mouri-san!

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.200
No wonder you're a renowned detective.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.700
No, you flatter me!

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.660
Say, Uncle ...

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:08.380
What does this "in the midst of where 26 letters fly about" mean?

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.750
Idiot!

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.380
Count the number of letters in the English words at the top.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:15.970
Romeo, Juliet, Victor, Bravo.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.140
They add up to 26 letters.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.050
Oh, I see!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.930
By the way, Juri-san ...

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.560
When will the performance of <i>Joséphine</i> run until?

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.690
Today is the last day.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.150
Which means what Kid is aiming for is ...

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.110
Ah-le-le!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.150
Geez!

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.280
What is it this time?

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.200
Because, it's strange!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.990
Look, there are only 22 letters.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.200
That can't be.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.750
I counted them as well.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.540
Even if you count the exclamation mark,
there are still three letters missing.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:51.210
Well, Kid must have counted wrong then ...

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:52.650
Hey, hey ...

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.010
Anyway ...

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.890
It's certain that Kid will be coming tonight to steal the jewel.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.020
Yes, I understand.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.690
There's another favor I must ask of you.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.690
Of course the police will be contacted as well, but ...

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.520
Would you also attend tonight's performance?

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:17.530
In order to protect this jewel from Kid.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.410
No problem.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.620
l, Mouri Kogorou ...

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:26.250
Have never turned down a request from a beautiful woman.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.370
Thank you so much!

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.250
Hey, Masayo-san.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.250
Oh, yes.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.470
These are tickets to tonight's performance.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.220
Please feel free to bring your companions along.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:42.680
Thank you.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:49.160
"In the midst of where 26 letters fly about" ...

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.210
"26 letters" should refer to the English alphabet ...

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.010
And this playing card ...

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.880
I can't quite picture it as a V sign ...

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.040
Shiodome View Tower

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.340
Sora Theatre

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.730
I'm so excited.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:12.640
Me too.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.770
Actually, I've wanted to see this play all along.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.360
Hey, Conan ...

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.480
What's with that backpack?

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:21.820
It's getting in the way.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:23.740
Just because ...

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.490
"Just because" of what?

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.370
Don't tell me ...

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.830
You brought snacks you weren't gonna share?

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.330
No way, I'm not you.

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:34.460
Hey, you guys.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.590
I specially invited you all here ...

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.000
So be on your best behavior, all right?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.860
Yes!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.680
Thanks for extending the invitation to us as well.

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:46.260
Of course!

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:48.970
Mouri-sensei!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:53.430
My apologies for having you wait!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.520
Yaguchi-san, hello.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:12:59.770
It's Yaguchi.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.900
Are you ready to see Mouri-sensei?

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:02.860
Sure.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:04.780
Come, please enter.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.240
Pardon our intrusion.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.700
Welcome, Mouri-san.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:09.870
Hello.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.770
I apologize for my appearance.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.650
Natsuki-chan, this is the famous Mouri Kogorou-san.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.810
You've heard him, right?

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.320
Sakai Natsuki

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.320
Hair Style & Make-up Artist

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:19.980
I'm Sakai Natsuki.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:21.340
Hello.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.800
So big!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.180
There are so many flowers!

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.640
Awesome!

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:31.430
I apologize.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:35.100
In accepting your offer, I may have taken too great an advantage
of your generosity by bringing these children along as well.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.940
No, I don't mind.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:41.520
Juri-san, are you into diving?

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.610
Yes, although I only just started.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.360
Would you like to go together sometime?

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:48.240
Sounds good.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:48.780
Sure!

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.370
Never mind that he's never dived before.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.000
Did you say something, Ran?

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.080
Nothing!

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.050
There are so many cosmetics!

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:06.590
Looks like it.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:12.600
This is called foundation, right?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.890
Just counting the foundation, there are ...

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.480
One, two, three, four ...

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.810
Five types.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:20.690
Five different types?

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:21.610
Hey, you!

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:24.570
You young ladies ...

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:28.030
It's too early for you to be interested in cosmetics!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.120
Kids should be kids ...

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:38.710
Right?

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.540
Yes, ma'am ...

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.000
Yes?

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.760
Oh, Masa-chan.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:53.850
Narusawa-san!

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.270
I heard Mouri-san was here ...

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:58.430
Mouri-san!

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.520
You're the renowned detective Mouri Kogorou-san, aren't you?

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.800
I am Narusawa.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.840
Narusawa Bunjirou

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.840
Actor

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.840
I'm a big fan of yours.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.720
A pleasure to meet you.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.820
Your role is that of Napoleon, is it not?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.590
Yes.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:14.700
You recognize the costume.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.120
Oh, yes!

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.160
Let me introduce everyone.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:18.160
Starting with ...

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:22.560
The actress playing the role of Joséphine's best
friend Thérésa Tallien, Tajima Tenko-san.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:24.110
Tajima Tenko

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:24.110
Actress

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.110
Nice to meet you.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.490
The one playing the role of Joséphine's lover
Hippolyte Charles, Shinjou Isao-kun.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:30.570
Shinjou Isao

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:30.570
Actor

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:29.990
Hello.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:36.870
And, our stage director on this play who's concurrently
playing the role of Joséphine's patron Paul Barras ...

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.160
Ban Tooru

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.180
Stage Director & Actor

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.370
The name's Ban Tooru.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.160
Pleasure to meet you.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.940
The pleasure is mine.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.770
Everybody's gathered here then?

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.480
Inspector Nakamori!

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:47.730
Hello, Mouri-san.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.490
Long time no <i>see</i>.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.570
I really have to thank you for <i>last</i> time.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.660
Oh no, I should really thank you.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.920
I wonder if they're all who they appear to be ...

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.350
You're right ...

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:20.850
Kid often disguises himself as someone close to his target.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.080
Perhaps he's already among us ...

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.650
Oh, yes ...

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:31.320
This time I've specially brought along
someone to help with the investigation ...

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:35.860
Well, I said there was no need, but that rascal Megure ...

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.120
Oh, no...

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.740
I mean <i>Inspector</i> Megure strongly recommended him.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.120
Get in here.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.560
Hello, I'm Kudou Shinichi.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:00.890
Shinichi?

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.100
Kudou-kun!

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:06.560
Oh, it's just this guy.

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:08.980
Isn't Kudou Shinichi ...

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:11.980
That famous high school detective?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:15.990
Who was he again?

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.450
What are you talking about?

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.700
He's Ran-oneesan's boyfriend!

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.450
He isn't!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:22.240
Her husband, actually.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:22.830
Sonoko!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.200
He's Kaitou Kid!

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.330
This person is not Shinichi-niichan!

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:29.880
It's Kid in disguise!

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:31.050
Kid?

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.090
And how would you know that?

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.260
Because I'm the real ...

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.050
The real—what?

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:40.800
Nothing ...

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.600
I see.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:47.060
We can't say that possibility doesn't exist ...

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.440
Ouch!

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.900
Please stop, Inspector Nakamori!

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:55.860
Just what is going on here?

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:56.820
I don't know.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.740
Maybe it's because Kid resembles me to begin with, or ...

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.910
Perhaps ...

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.330
You're the one that's an imposter.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.290
Hey, hey...

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.330
All right!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:08.790
Ow!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.250
There's no doubt he's the real thing.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:14.510
Now, I'll go ahead and pinch the faces of everyone else as well.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:19.180
No, there's no need for that.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:23.010
I have a feeling that Kid is not among us.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.270
I'm telling you, he is!

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:29.650
And I've already thought of a secret plan to arrest Kid.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:33.980
Well then, please share this secret plan of yours.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:39.320
Maki-san, if you don't mind, can we have
everyone else out of the room for a moment?

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:42.120
I don't mind, Inspector.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.620
We've already finished up our preparations.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:45.740
Excuse me.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.370
I'm going to go do things my own way, so ...

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:50.540
What'd you say?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.290
Wonderful!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.630
We've got no use for detective brats like you.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.640
Well then, we shall take our leave.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.520
We look forward to seeing you on stage.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:11.770
Hey ...

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.280
You should have called me if you were going to be coming back!

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.320
Sorry, sorry.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.860
I just wanted to see that cute face you make when you get surprised.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:21.820
Cute...?

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:24.410
Starting out rather boldly, aren't you?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:29.790
Well, I guess I'll go and check the roof.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.920
Ran, would you like to come along?

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.840
The top floor is like an observation deck.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:39.210
You should go, Ran.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.380
I wanna go, too!

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:41.720
You will stay here.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.050
I wanna go, I wanna go!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.970
I wanna go, too!

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:44.950
Now look here, you ...

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.560
I wanna go, wanna go, wanna go!

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.520
All right.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.850
Why don't we all go together?

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.330
Yay!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.480
Say, isn't Conan ...

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:58.530
He seems to be a completely different person around Ran-san.

00:19:58.530 --> 00:19:59.530
It must be because ...

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.030
He's at that age where he's spoiled.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:03.110
I see.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.620
What a brat, that guy.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.220
Don't forget you're brats too.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.730
It's not like I'd let her be alone with Kid.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.390
All right, looks like this door's really locked.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:39.530
How'd it go?

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:43.610
All the doors to the roof are locked.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:48.410
In other words, if my deduction is correct ...

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.500
Kid won't <i>kid </i>around with us via the roof!

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:54.870
I guess not ...

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.020
Because he's already here.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:06.760
Hey ...

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.720
I'll watch Conan-kun, so ...

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:11.720
Why don't you two go off somewhere?

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:12.980
No, it's fine.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:14.520
Besides ...

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:17.810
He seems different somehow ...

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:23.190
Because, he never says things like that.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:24.150
Like what?

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.620
Cute, for example.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:33.370
That just means he's gotten a little more straightforward.

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:35.160
You should be more frank as well.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.120
If you like him, just tell him.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:38.880
No way!

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.040
I told you, it’s not like that, didn't I?

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:45.010
Awesome, awesome, awesome!

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:48.640
Genta-kun, you've only been saying ''awesome" this whole time.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:50.350
What else can I say?

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:51.510
It's awesome.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.270
Oh, look at this—what a superb view!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.440
There's really not much else to say besides ''awesome".

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:00.060
See?

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:04.190
It really is impressive, isn't it?

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:08.660
How daring of him ...

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.950
To disguise as Shinichi, of all people.

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:12.870
Yeah.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:16.290
Maybe it's because it's easier for him
to reach his goal by disguising as me.

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:19.040
At least it saves us time searching for him.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:20.000
Yeah.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.630
By the way, you guys ...

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:25.300
Do you know who Napoleon was?

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:26.880
Yeah, sort of.

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:31.390
At least that he's the French hero who
conquered Europe for a period of time.

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:32.600
All right!

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:35.020
Then, as a warm-up for the performance ...

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:37.310
I'll give you a quiz on Napoleon!

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:39.850
Shinichi-oniisan's going to?

00:22:40.310 --> 00:22:42.560
Just like Professor Agasa.

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:44.110
It's not going to be a lame pun, right?

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:49.030
My question is grounded in history, so it's educational.

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:51.030
You should think on it too, kid!

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.680
Shut up.

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:54.950
Ready?

00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:56.660
On Napoleon's land ...

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:58.710
Two Japanese people built their houses.

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:02.040
Who were those two Japanese people, out of the following choices?

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:04.000
One, Fuyuno-san.

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:05.960
Two, Furuno-san.

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:08.050
Three, Fukano-san.

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:13.600
Fuyuno-san, Furuno-san, Fukano-san ...

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:15.390
All the names have 'fu' and 'no' in them.

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:17.220
I got it!

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:19.520
Don't tell them!

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:24.480
The difference between the three names is
that they have 'yu', 'ru', and 'ka' in the middle ...

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:26.020
I got it!

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:27.440
It's Fuyuno-san and Furuno-san!

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:31.530
Only Fukano-san's name has 'ka' in the middle, right?

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.760
'Ka' in the 'middle'
translates to 'Chinese'

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.550
"N A K A   G A   K A"

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.550
"KA (カ) IN
THE MIDDLE

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.550
"IN OTHER WORDS:
"CENTRAL KA
(CHUUKA)"

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.550
"CHUUKA (CHUUGOKU NO KOTO)"
"CHINESE (PERTAINING TO CHINA)"

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:36.240
Therefore Fukano-san is Chinese!

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:41.870
What?

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:43.130
Are you saying that's not the answer?

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:46.500
The answer is correct, but it's the way you solved it.

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:53.090
Guys, do you know Napoleon's famous quote,
"In my dictionary, the word impossible does not exist''?

00:23:54.220 --> 00:23:55.010
I've heard of it!

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:58.850
This riddle plays upon that famous quote.

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:01.480
"Land" can also be pronounced 'jisho' (dictionary).

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.040
LAND (TOCHI)

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.040
LAND (JISHO)

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:09.260
FUKANO

00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:04.100
'Moji' refers to the characters
posted for the name on a doorplate.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:09.280
IN MY DICTIONARY, THE WORD
IMPOSSIBLE DOES NOT EXIST

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:09.280
ON MY LAND, THE CHARACTERS
FUKANO DO NOT APPEAR

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:08.170
Basically: "On my land, the
characters Fukano do not appear".

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:10.860
I see.

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:13.930
By the way, what Napoleon actually said was ...

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:18.010
"Impossible is a word found only in a fool's dictionary".

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:19.220
Or so it seems.

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:22.660
As expected from the amazing Haibara-san!

00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:24.540
But, it's still just a lame pun, as we thought.

00:24:24.540 --> 00:24:25.580
Besides ...

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:27.920
I don't think it was very educational either.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:29.760
Really?

00:25:25.310 --> 00:25:26.560
Joséphine ...

00:25:26.560 --> 00:25:27.270
Thérésa ...

00:25:29.230 --> 00:25:31.150
What is it, Citizen Barras?

00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:33.490
Sir, allow me to introduce ...

00:25:33.940 --> 00:25:36.610
Thérésa Tallien, and Joséphine.

00:25:36.610 --> 00:25:37.320
This gentleman is...

00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:39.070
I know of him.

00:25:39.570 --> 00:25:42.490
General Napoleon Bonaparte.

00:25:42.490 --> 00:25:45.040
I heard you were a very heroic gentleman.

00:25:45.370 --> 00:25:47.250
You flatter me.

00:25:47.790 --> 00:25:51.250
General, I wonder if you would dance with me?

00:25:51.250 --> 00:25:52.250
With pleasure.

00:26:51.770 --> 00:26:54.320
Everything around me makes me miss ...

00:26:55.610 --> 00:26:58.070
Those glorious days ...

00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:00.200
Bonaparte ...

00:27:01.280 --> 00:27:02.070
The Isle of Elba ...

00:27:03.490 --> 00:27:04.410
The King of the Romans ...

00:27:34.020 --> 00:27:34.900
Hey, Ran.

00:27:35.980 --> 00:27:38.990
Isn't that person next to the Pope your father?

00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:49.730
So that's the secret plan to catch Kid?

00:27:55.420 --> 00:27:56.630
Haibara, cover for me.

00:27:58.670 --> 00:27:59.840
Have fun.

00:28:19.690 --> 00:28:20.940
Kid, you all right?

00:28:21.570 --> 00:28:22.950
That was pretty dangerous.

00:28:23.360 --> 00:28:25.030
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:28:25.030 --> 00:28:25.820
Anyway ...

00:28:25.820 --> 00:28:26.870
Is something the matter?

00:28:29.740 --> 00:28:31.960
This kid suddenly came running from around the corner ...

00:28:32.410 --> 00:28:34.790
He fell down after crashing into me.

00:28:36.580 --> 00:28:37.750
Are you all right, little boy?

00:28:38.550 --> 00:28:39.590
I'm fine!

00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:42.880
But, mister, your baton is really something!

00:28:43.380 --> 00:28:45.970
Isn't it longer than the one this man has?

00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:47.550
You're right.

00:28:47.550 --> 00:28:48.720
It's much longer.

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:51.810
Well, there are many different sorts of batons.

00:28:51.810 --> 00:28:53.520
Length: 60 centimeters or below.

00:28:53.520 --> 00:28:55.440
Diameter: 3 centimeters or below.

00:28:55.440 --> 00:28:57.610
Weight: 320 grams or below.

00:28:58.360 --> 00:29:02.900
Those are the regulations on batons mandated by the public safety
commissions in each of Japan's administrative regions, right?

00:29:03.610 --> 00:29:05.530
Mister, isn't yours ...

00:29:05.530 --> 00:29:07.120
Quite a bit too long?

00:29:09.240 --> 00:29:10.700
Tell me, why is that?

00:29:14.790 --> 00:29:17.630
As for why it's so long ...

00:29:17.630 --> 00:29:18.500
That's because ...

00:29:19.040 --> 00:29:20.460
It's not a baton!

00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:27.640
I won't let you get away!

00:29:30.680 --> 00:29:31.600
Wait!

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:35.020
Damn!

00:29:50.830 --> 00:29:52.830
Everything in the world ...

00:29:53.830 --> 00:29:54.580
Glory.

00:29:55.330 --> 00:29:56.210
Victory.

00:29:56.960 --> 00:29:58.830
The future is mine!

00:29:59.170 --> 00:30:01.590
It is ours!

00:30:30.370 --> 00:30:32.580
When the curtains are completely lowered, we strike.

00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:33.540
Understood.

00:30:42.130 --> 00:30:42.960
Now!

00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:44.050
Grab Kid!

00:30:44.250 --> 00:30:45.550
He's disguised as Napoleon!

00:30:48.800 --> 00:30:49.340
Hey!

00:30:49.340 --> 00:30:49.880
What are you ...

00:30:55.390 --> 00:30:57.020
How careless, Kid.

00:30:57.680 --> 00:30:59.600
That underwhelming code you sent ...

00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:02.560
Yours truly, Mouri Kogorou-sama, deciphered every last bit of it!

00:31:03.380 --> 00:31:04.000
No!

00:31:04.020 --> 00:31:04.820
I'm not Kid!

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:08.070
Cut the nonsense and show us your true form ...

00:31:08.070 --> 00:31:09.280
Kaitou Kid!

00:31:09.950 --> 00:31:11.660
Ow, ow, ow!

00:31:17.450 --> 00:31:18.120
He's real.

00:31:18.870 --> 00:31:20.960
Then, where's Kid?

00:31:34.760 --> 00:31:37.140
Let's end this game here ...

00:31:37.140 --> 00:31:38.270
Mr. Sneak-Thief.

00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:40.690
We should.

00:31:42.730 --> 00:31:46.480
It's growing too dark to continue playing hide-and-seek with you ...

00:31:52.910 --> 00:31:53.990
Detective-kun.

00:31:55.780 --> 00:31:58.080
Enough with the small talk.

00:31:59.370 --> 00:32:01.870
Let's bring this to a <i>Kick</i>ing end.

00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:06.290
Yeah.

00:32:06.290 --> 00:32:09.130
After all, your girl is waiting with your prepared supper.

00:32:09.800 --> 00:32:10.800
Conan-kun!

00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:13.970
Supper's ready!

00:32:16.260 --> 00:32:18.260
If you don't hurry, it'll all be gone!

00:32:39.370 --> 00:32:42.000
Well, it does seem like the end is near ...

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:43.210
Detective-kun.

00:32:43.790 --> 00:32:45.000
Yeah.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:46.170
Seems that way.

00:33:22.410 --> 00:33:23.080
Hey, hey ...

00:33:29.630 --> 00:33:31.050
I see.

00:33:31.050 --> 00:33:33.800
A paraglider for a hang glider, huh?

00:34:35.460 --> 00:34:36.340
I expected as much from you.

00:34:37.240 --> 00:34:39.030
The paraglider just now ...

00:34:39.030 --> 00:34:40.740
Was it another of Professor Agasa's inventions?

00:34:41.160 --> 00:34:42.990
You've got nowhere left to run.

00:34:43.450 --> 00:34:45.040
Without flight ...

00:34:45.040 --> 00:34:47.210
Even Kaitou Kid is just an ordinary sneak-thief.

00:34:51.580 --> 00:34:53.040
Then I guess it's time ...

00:34:53.040 --> 00:34:55.710
I return to being the thief I was.

00:34:56.740 --> 00:34:57.860
What's that noise?

00:35:00.610 --> 00:35:01.370
No!

00:35:06.430 --> 00:35:07.390
Later!

00:35:15.690 --> 00:35:16.900
Damn it!

00:35:32.060 --> 00:35:34.690
And now for the weather around the airports ...

00:35:32.900 --> 00:35:37.360
Haneda Airport

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:36.400
Hokkaido ...

00:35:37.610 --> 00:35:43.320
Tonight in hakodate, there will be rain, at times turning
into thunderstorm, and winds from the southwest.

00:35:43.590 --> 00:35:45.510
Thunderstorms in Hakodate, huh?

00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:47.560
Such unfortunate weather.

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:50.020
What if the airplane is struck by lightning?

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:51.810
It's all right!

00:35:51.810 --> 00:35:54.110
Because planes fly above the clouds.

00:35:54.110 --> 00:35:57.070
Oh, but the landing takes place below the clouds, doesn't it?

00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:02.990
I got all dressed up for today and it's going to rain ...

00:36:03.450 --> 00:36:07.160
In that getup, you'll get your belly button taken by the God of Thunder ...

00:36:07.160 --> 00:36:08.450
My grandmama said so!

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:10.410
Really?

00:36:10.830 --> 00:36:12.620
Then, I dare him to try and take it if he can!

00:36:16.250 --> 00:36:18.500
You've shown us too much kindness.

00:36:18.920 --> 00:36:22.470
Even going as far as inviting us to attend
the post-performance celebration party.

00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:27.930
It was thanks to everyone that the gemstone is safe, so it's only proper.

00:36:28.220 --> 00:36:29.520
Exactly.

00:36:29.520 --> 00:36:32.390
Rather than dwelling on that, let's enjoy Hakodate!

00:36:32.940 --> 00:36:35.400
You know, that Juri sure is late ...

00:36:36.020 --> 00:36:36.860
Yeah.

00:36:37.440 --> 00:36:38.650
Sorry about that.

00:36:38.650 --> 00:36:41.150
She's having Natsuki-san do her make-up right now.

00:36:41.570 --> 00:36:43.570
In the car parked in the parking lot.

00:36:43.570 --> 00:36:44.950
Applying make-up?

00:36:44.950 --> 00:36:47.530
It sure is tough being a huge star.

00:36:47.740 --> 00:36:49.950
The real burden is on Natsuki-chan.

00:36:50.950 --> 00:36:56.420
Juri finds her so useful that she's pretty
much her personal assistant nowadays.

00:36:57.840 --> 00:36:59.150
I see.

00:36:59.190 --> 00:37:00.230
Hi!

00:37:01.340 --> 00:37:03.090
Sorry for the wait everyone.

00:37:03.260 --> 00:37:06.930
My, as always, you're exceptionally beautiful today!

00:37:07.350 --> 00:37:08.930
Thank you, Mouri-san.

00:37:09.470 --> 00:37:11.020
It looks like everyone has arrived.

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:13.390
No, Shinjou-kun isn't here yet.

00:37:14.390 --> 00:37:16.560
Shinjou-san isn't feeling well.

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:18.730
He called this morning to say he couldn't make it.

00:37:19.230 --> 00:37:20.650
Oh, is that so?

00:37:20.650 --> 00:37:22.400
Such a pity, isn't it, Juri?

00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:23.610
Why's that?

00:37:24.900 --> 00:37:25.700
Nothing.

00:37:28.740 --> 00:37:30.030
Uhm ...

00:37:30.450 --> 00:37:32.700
Aren't the other cast members coming?

00:37:33.370 --> 00:37:35.120
Of course not!

00:37:35.120 --> 00:37:38.170
There's no merit in asking those extras to come along.

00:37:52.950 --> 00:37:54.080
What was that just now?

00:38:02.460 --> 00:38:05.930
Hakodate Lake Oonuma Shoreside

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:10.390
Juri's Villa

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:20.290
If my instincts are correct, that guy will definitely show up here.

00:38:22.130 --> 00:38:24.800
Inspector Nakamori, all personnel are present.

00:38:24.800 --> 00:38:25.380
Good.

00:38:26.220 --> 00:38:27.550
A-Team, take the front.

00:38:27.550 --> 00:38:28.680
B-Team, take the rear.

00:38:28.680 --> 00:38:30.430
C-Team, patrol the vicinity.

00:38:30.430 --> 00:38:30.970
Yes, sir!

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:35.060
Inspector Nakamori ...

00:38:35.060 --> 00:38:35.470
What is it?

00:38:36.310 --> 00:38:37.690
Inside the villa, the lights ...

00:38:37.690 --> 00:38:38.020
What?

00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:45.820
That's ...

00:39:03.820 --> 00:39:07.110
Sky Japan Airlines, leaving for Hakodate.

00:39:07.110 --> 00:39:08.990
Flight 865 departing at 18:15 ...

00:39:09.490 --> 00:39:15.120
Is now commencing with boarding procedures.

00:39:15.540 --> 00:39:20.370
Calling all Flight 865 passengers headed for Hakodate ...

00:39:30.990 --> 00:39:33.160
Wow, they're so soft and fluffy!

00:39:33.700 --> 00:39:35.660
Not bad, right?

00:39:35.990 --> 00:39:37.750
I feel like a CEO!

00:39:37.750 --> 00:39:40.920
As far as domestic flights, having a First Class second floor ...

00:39:40.920 --> 00:39:43.380
Is exclusive to Sky Japan Airlines!

00:40:00.940 --> 00:40:02.020
Hey, what is it?

00:40:03.230 --> 00:40:04.480
What's wrong, Ran?

00:40:04.480 --> 00:40:06.480
You've been looking behind you ever since we got on.

00:40:07.820 --> 00:40:08.730
It's nothing.

00:40:08.730 --> 00:40:09.900
Welcome aboard.

00:40:09.900 --> 00:40:10.440
Thank you.

00:40:11.150 --> 00:40:11.900
She's here!

00:40:12.950 --> 00:40:13.950
Who's here?

00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:15.240
Be quiet.

00:40:16.870 --> 00:40:18.620
Uhm, the seat next to you ...

00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:20.660
Oh, go ahead.

00:40:21.940 --> 00:40:22.650
Eri!

00:40:23.520 --> 00:40:24.270
You!

00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:25.500
Auntie?

00:40:26.920 --> 00:40:27.960
Ah-le-le!

00:40:27.960 --> 00:40:30.010
Mom, don't tell me you're going to Hakodate too?

00:40:30.340 --> 00:40:32.300
What a wonderful coincidence!

00:40:32.300 --> 00:40:35.890
It's definitely fate that brought you and Dad together again.

00:40:35.890 --> 00:40:36.970
What are you talking about?

00:40:37.510 --> 00:40:40.500
You were the one who said you were invited by Juri-san to Hakodate

00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:42.770
and asked me to accompany you due to your father being busy.

00:40:42.770 --> 00:40:44.350
Ran, not this from you again ...

00:40:44.560 --> 00:40:46.020
Now, now ...

00:40:46.020 --> 00:40:47.820
Anyway, why don't you two have a seat?

00:40:48.020 --> 00:40:49.570
You've got to be kidding! 
You've got to be kidding!

00:40:49.570 --> 00:40:51.610
Why do I have to sit next to him!? 
Why do I have to sit next to her!?

00:40:53.280 --> 00:40:55.110
Come on, you two ...

00:40:56.160 --> 00:40:57.240
Dad!

00:40:58.030 --> 00:40:59.830
Excuse me, Juri-san ...

00:40:59.830 --> 00:41:01.120
May I sit next to you?

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:03.080
Sure, go ahead.

00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:04.420
Geez ...

00:41:05.710 --> 00:41:07.040
Wait, Mom!

00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:11.670
Excuse me—you're Maki Juri-san, correct?

00:41:11.670 --> 00:41:12.590
Yes.

00:41:12.590 --> 00:41:15.090
My name is Kisaki Eri.

00:41:15.090 --> 00:41:18.970
I want to thank you for inviting me for this occasion.

00:41:19.760 --> 00:41:20.260
No problem.

00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:27.690
That's right!

00:41:27.690 --> 00:41:31.900
If the vulgar man next to you troubles you with his speech or conduct ...

00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:33.820
Don't hesitate to ask for my consultation.

00:41:36.240 --> 00:41:37.450
You're a lawyer.

00:41:37.780 --> 00:41:39.070
Well then, I shall be at your service.

00:41:39.620 --> 00:41:40.120
Sure.

00:41:51.340 --> 00:41:53.090
How did things end up being like this?

00:41:53.360 --> 00:41:54.530
"End up being"?

00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:55.700
Get used to it.

00:41:59.510 --> 00:42:00.600
Hello, everyone!

00:42:00.600 --> 00:42:01.970
Sorry to have kept you all waiting.

00:42:01.970 --> 00:42:02.930
Shinjou-san!

00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:07.020
Didn't you say that you weren't coming because you were feeling ill?

00:42:07.190 --> 00:42:07.900
Nah ...

00:42:08.230 --> 00:42:10.020
I'm feeling much better.

00:42:10.310 --> 00:42:11.860
I was just sitting around by myself ...

00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:14.860
So I figured I would join you guys.

00:42:17.950 --> 00:42:20.700
Sorry to keep you waiting, Joséphine-sama.

00:42:21.830 --> 00:42:23.620
Why haven't you done as I said?

00:42:24.040 --> 00:42:25.120
Relax.

00:42:25.620 --> 00:42:27.750
There'll be more than enough time once we get there.

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:32.000
Well, have a safe trip.

00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:33.170
Yes, see you again soon!

00:42:37.030 --> 00:42:41.330
Flight attendats, please prepare the cabin for daparture.

00:42:46.390 --> 00:42:47.810
What are you thinking about?

00:42:49.310 --> 00:42:51.650
I bet it has something to do with Kid.

00:42:51.650 --> 00:42:52.440
Yeah.

00:42:53.110 --> 00:42:57.030
Did he truly intend to steal the jewel last night?

00:42:58.630 --> 00:43:02.260
It's growing too dark to continue playing hide-and-seek with you ...

00:43:02.260 --> 00:43:03.470
Detective-kun.

00:43:04.700 --> 00:43:08.290
On top of that, he had an overly long baton stick.

00:43:08.290 --> 00:43:09.870
That's too careless a mistake for Kid.

00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:11.500
Hey, hey!

00:43:12.000 --> 00:43:13.790
My seat number is 4K.

00:43:13.790 --> 00:43:15.250
K for Kid, right?

00:43:15.250 --> 00:43:17.920
My seat number is 4J.

00:43:17.920 --> 00:43:19.130
J for Jumbo, isn't it?

00:43:19.510 --> 00:43:22.640
My seat number is 4B.

00:43:23.390 --> 00:43:25.100
That means ... that means ...

00:43:25.990 --> 00:43:26.910
So that's it!

00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:31.020
The four English words that Kid wrote on his message ...

00:43:31.020 --> 00:43:32.900
They were a reference to the phonetic alphabet!

00:43:33.770 --> 00:43:34.820
Phonetic alphabet?

00:43:35.110 --> 00:43:35.480
Yeah.

00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:40.320
They're codes used over wireless communication
in order to prevent miscommunication.

00:43:40.320 --> 00:43:41.860
'R' becomes 'Romeo'.

00:43:41.860 --> 00:43:43.410
'J' becomes 'Juliet'.

00:43:43.410 --> 00:43:45.010
'V' becomes 'Victor'.

00:43:45.010 --> 00:43:46.770
'B' becomes 'Bravo'.

00:43:47.290 --> 00:43:50.920
Airplanes also use it over radio communications.

00:43:52.310 --> 00:43:54.110
SKY-J 865.

00:43:54.440 --> 00:43:56.980
Runway 16 Left.

00:43:56.980 --> 00:43:58.070
Taxi in.

00:43:58.210 --> 00:44:02.050
JULIET 10, ECHO 10, CHARLIE 10.

00:44:02.490 --> 00:44:04.580
SKY-J 865.

00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:08.020
JULIET 10, ECHO 10, CHARLIE 10.

00:44:08.350 --> 00:44:12.520
In essence, the ''In the midst of where 26 letters fly about” part ...

00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:17.230
Was an advance notice that he's going to commit the crime aboard
the plane, where those phonetic codes fly about over the airwaves.

00:44:17.440 --> 00:44:22.150
Furthermore, it will take place on this flight, from Tokyo to Hakodate.

00:44:22.150 --> 00:44:23.200
Why is that?

00:44:23.200 --> 00:44:25.200
If it's on plane, the return trip ...

00:44:26.580 --> 00:44:27.660
The picture of the playing card, right?

00:44:27.990 --> 00:44:28.620
Yeah.

00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:32.120
That the two of spades card was split in half ...

00:44:32.830 --> 00:44:36.630
Indicates a number that is not divisible by 2—an odd number.

00:44:37.250 --> 00:44:42.300
Flights that depart from Tokyo are, like this flight
numbered 865, given odd number designations.

00:44:42.300 --> 00:44:44.890
All flights arriving into Tokyo are designated even numbers.

00:44:45.430 --> 00:44:48.640
If we think about it that way, we can
understand what happened last night.

00:44:49.220 --> 00:44:51.560
He purposely drew my attention to him ...

00:44:51.560 --> 00:44:53.730
To lure me into thinking his heist had failed and ...

00:44:53.730 --> 00:44:56.150
Put everyone off their guard, as he intended.

00:44:57.110 --> 00:44:58.520
If that's the case ...

00:44:59.480 --> 00:45:01.990
Kid is somewhere on this plane.

00:45:02.280 --> 00:45:04.610
And even now is aiming to steal that ring.

00:45:09.200 --> 00:45:10.910
Is anything wrong?

00:45:10.910 --> 00:45:12.830
For some reason, I'm not feeling too well.

00:45:13.040 --> 00:45:14.920
You must be getting tired.

00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:20.070
This flight is Sky Japan Airline Flight 865, headed for Hakodate Airport.

00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:18.170
Here, Juri, put your hand out.

00:45:18.170 --> 00:45:19.210
Some vitamin pills.

00:45:24.030 --> 00:45:28.200
I am your chief cabin attendant, Shindou.

00:45:29.720 --> 00:45:36.060
SKY-J 865. Winds 160 and 10. Clear for takeoff.

00:45:36.310 --> 00:45:42.150
SKY-J 865. Clear for takeoff. Runway 16 Left.

00:45:43.900 --> 00:45:44.780
Takeoff.

00:45:53.200 --> 00:45:53.660
Eighty.

00:45:54.330 --> 00:45:54.910
Check.

00:45:58.770 --> 00:45:59.860
V1.

00:46:00.980 --> 00:46:01.980
VR.

00:46:05.570 --> 00:46:06.410
V2.

00:46:07.130 --> 00:46:07.890
Positive.

00:46:08.950 --> 00:46:09.830
Gear up.

00:46:10.140 --> 00:46:11.260
Gear up.

00:46:28.360 --> 00:46:29.030
Huh?

00:46:29.570 --> 00:46:31.370
My ears feel weird for some reason.

00:46:31.740 --> 00:46:33.790
Yeah, me too ...

00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:35.580
It's because of the change in air pressure.

00:46:35.580 --> 00:46:37.210
Just swallow and you'll be fine.

00:46:40.830 --> 00:46:42.090
It still feels weird.

00:46:45.510 --> 00:46:46.840
Nothing happened.

00:46:46.840 --> 00:46:50.340
If that's the case, hold your nose and blow.

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:54.140
However, don't do it too hard.

00:46:54.140 --> 00:46:55.720
You might get dizzy.

00:46:59.560 --> 00:47:00.730
It worked!

00:47:00.730 --> 00:47:02.610
Awesome, look—something came out.

00:47:06.610 --> 00:47:08.400
Conan-kun, face forward, all right?

00:47:12.530 --> 00:47:14.030
You were right, it worked!

00:47:15.290 --> 00:47:16.790
I guess girls will be girls ...

00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:23.540
The way someone looks when blowing
their nose isn't very attractive, you know?

00:47:23.540 --> 00:47:28.090
She wouldn't want someone of the opposite
gender, especially someone she likes, to see that.

00:47:43.690 --> 00:47:45.150
Excuse me, Juri-san.

00:47:46.150 --> 00:47:48.400
Could you sign this for me as a commemoration?

00:47:49.650 --> 00:47:50.610
Sure.

00:47:53.660 --> 00:47:55.030
Oh, damn it ...

00:47:55.030 --> 00:47:56.910
I forgot to bring a pen for you to sign it with.

00:47:56.910 --> 00:47:57.490
Maki-san?

00:47:58.500 --> 00:48:00.000
Here, use this.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:01.080
Thank you.

00:48:01.620 --> 00:48:03.830
You can see how I could never let her out of my reach.

00:48:08.760 --> 00:48:11.260
What's Dad doing?

00:48:11.260 --> 00:48:14.260
Don't worry about that superficial man.

00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:17.140
How about taking this time to tell me who everyone is?

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:31.570
Sorry 'bout that.

00:48:32.030 --> 00:48:32.910
Are you all right?

00:48:33.030 --> 00:48:33.610
Yeah.

00:48:40.040 --> 00:48:40.750
All done.

00:48:40.750 --> 00:48:42.460
Thank you very much!

00:48:51.170 --> 00:48:54.130
Western or Japanese snacks—which would you like?

00:48:54.130 --> 00:48:55.550
No, I'm fine.

00:48:57.050 --> 00:48:58.220
Western or Japanese snacks ...

00:48:58.470 --> 00:49:00.180
I won't need either.

00:49:00.180 --> 00:49:01.520
Nor any drinks.

00:49:01.850 --> 00:49:04.190
I'll take beer and a Japanese snack to go with it.

00:49:04.520 --> 00:49:06.360
Just a moment, please.

00:49:10.360 --> 00:49:12.280
Drinking beer in first class is the ...

00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:32.460
Hakodate Airport

00:49:35.970 --> 00:49:37.680
This rain is horrible, isn't it?

00:49:37.680 --> 00:49:38.550
Yeah ...

00:49:39.010 --> 00:49:41.140
Hopefully everything will be all right.

00:49:42.270 --> 00:49:46.060
SKY-J 865, contact Tokyo Control.

00:49:46.520 --> 00:49:48.690
118.90.

00:49:48.980 --> 00:49:51.110
SKY-J 865.

00:49:51.320 --> 00:49:54.240
118.90.

00:49:55.650 --> 00:49:59.780
Tokyo Control, SKY-J 865.

00:49:59.780 --> 00:50:02.290
Flight level: 390.

00:50:02.450 --> 00:50:06.790
SKY-J 865, Tokyo Control. Roger.

00:50:07.290 --> 00:50:09.040
Are you all right, Captain?

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:10.170
I'm fine.

00:50:10.170 --> 00:50:13.130
Last night my youngest had a fever, so I didn't really sleep much.

00:50:13.670 --> 00:50:15.470
Should I request some coffee for you?

00:50:16.590 --> 00:50:18.340
Please, if you would.

00:50:28.650 --> 00:50:30.270
The ring's still all right?

00:50:30.270 --> 00:50:30.860
Yeah.

00:50:31.650 --> 00:50:33.400
But I won't let my guard down.

00:50:41.850 --> 00:50:43.220
That was rather quick.

00:50:43.410 --> 00:50:44.370
Hey, Masayo-san.

00:50:45.540 --> 00:50:46.540
The chocolates ...

00:50:52.440 --> 00:50:54.070
Service for the cockpit?

00:50:54.570 --> 00:50:56.440
Relatively rare on domestic routes.

00:51:01.220 --> 00:51:02.260
It's Misawa.

00:51:02.260 --> 00:51:03.930
I've brought the coffee.

00:51:04.290 --> 00:51:05.040
Please come in.

00:51:10.020 --> 00:51:11.360
Sorry for the intrusion.

00:51:14.190 --> 00:51:15.730
You can't come in here, Miss!

00:51:15.730 --> 00:51:17.030
It's fine, Misawa-kun.

00:51:18.950 --> 00:51:20.570
She's your senior.

00:51:21.990 --> 00:51:23.450
Long time no see, Captain!

00:51:23.660 --> 00:51:24.410
Yeah.

00:51:24.410 --> 00:51:26.910
It's been about five years since you resigned, hasn't it?

00:51:27.040 --> 00:51:28.790
Seven years now.

00:51:28.790 --> 00:51:30.170
It's been that long?

00:51:30.750 --> 00:51:32.380
You too, Nakaya-san, long time no see.

00:51:32.560 --> 00:51:33.480
Hey.

00:51:33.500 --> 00:51:35.090
I saw Joséphine, you know.

00:51:35.090 --> 00:51:36.090
Oh, I'm glad!

00:51:36.250 --> 00:51:38.590
Yeah, it was truly wonderful.

00:51:38.590 --> 00:51:39.760
Really?

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:41.220
Thank you so much.

00:51:41.680 --> 00:51:43.720
We will always come in support of you.

00:52:00.150 --> 00:52:02.530
Well then, Captain, I'll see you later.

00:52:06.490 --> 00:52:07.200
Maki-san?

00:52:08.250 --> 00:52:09.660
Here, have a chocolate.

00:52:09.660 --> 00:52:10.460
Thank you.

00:52:13.170 --> 00:52:14.710
Mouri-sensei, would you like one too?

00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:17.110
Oh, thank you.

00:52:19.570 --> 00:52:20.950
Yum!

00:52:55.500 --> 00:52:56.540
It can't be!

00:52:58.340 --> 00:53:00.340
Uncle, there's an almond scent.

00:53:01.380 --> 00:53:02.170
Yeah.

00:53:02.170 --> 00:53:03.760
Cyanide poisoning, then.

00:53:04.130 --> 00:53:05.300
It's the chocolate!

00:53:05.300 --> 00:53:07.140
There was poison in the chocolates!

00:53:07.760 --> 00:53:08.680
The chocolates?

00:53:11.640 --> 00:53:12.640
Dad!

00:53:13.190 --> 00:53:14.640
Don't worry.

00:53:14.640 --> 00:53:19.520
If there had been poison in the chocolate Uncle ate,
the symptoms would have already manifested.

00:53:21.460 --> 00:53:22.380
But then ...

00:53:22.380 --> 00:53:23.760
How did Juri-san ...

00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:42.880
The Captain's message was ...

00:53:42.880 --> 00:53:45.090
In order not to alarm the other passengers ...

00:53:45.090 --> 00:53:49.600
He'd like for news of this incident to not be
leaked until after we arrive at the airport.

00:53:49.890 --> 00:53:51.010
Understood.

00:53:52.220 --> 00:53:57.150
But, just how did the culprit manage to poison Juri-san?

00:53:57.520 --> 00:54:00.110
Like I said, it must have been in the chocolates.

00:54:00.110 --> 00:54:02.400
Since she collapsed right afer eating it.

00:54:03.190 --> 00:54:04.400
I'm with him on this one.

00:54:05.030 --> 00:54:05.610
No way!

00:54:05.950 --> 00:54:07.530
Don't look at me!

00:54:07.530 --> 00:54:11.200
I bought this box of chocolates this afternoon
from a shop in Ginza where we always get them!

00:54:11.200 --> 00:54:13.410
And I only just now opened them!

00:54:13.410 --> 00:54:14.370
Right, Natsuki-san?

00:54:15.870 --> 00:54:18.170
Sorry, I wasn't really watching.

00:54:18.170 --> 00:54:19.080
Natsuki-san!

00:54:19.460 --> 00:54:22.500
But, since you ate one too and nothing happened ...

00:54:22.500 --> 00:54:25.380
That means that only a portion of the chocolate was poisoned, right?

00:54:26.010 --> 00:54:31.260
If that's so, I wonder how Juri-san was made
to choose one of the poisoned chocolates?

00:54:31.260 --> 00:54:35.850
As her manager, it's only natural you would
know which chocolate she'd eat first.

00:54:36.060 --> 00:54:37.770
I didn't do it!

00:54:37.770 --> 00:54:40.810
Besides, she chooses the chocolate randomly every time!

00:54:41.060 --> 00:54:45.320
It did look like Juri-san hesitated over which chocolate to choose.

00:54:46.440 --> 00:54:47.200
Shut up!

00:54:47.200 --> 00:54:48.240
Kids should stay out of this!

00:54:50.030 --> 00:54:52.990
At any rate, I will take possession of those chocolates.

00:54:53.540 --> 00:54:54.240
Yes, sir.

00:54:55.040 --> 00:54:58.710
As for the rest, we can only wait until we arrive
at the airport and let the police deal with it.

00:54:58.710 --> 00:54:59.330
Yeah.

00:55:00.040 --> 00:55:04.250
In order to preserve the crime scene, would
everyone please move to the seats at the back?

00:55:05.300 --> 00:55:08.470
The front lavatory is now off limits as well.

00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:27.130
Apart from that chocolate, all that's come into
contact with her mouth since she boarded were ...

00:55:28.550 --> 00:55:29.800
Those vitamin pills ...

00:55:32.260 --> 00:55:33.680
Even so ...

00:55:33.680 --> 00:55:36.270
It wasn't a sure thing that Juri-san
would have wanted to take those pills.

00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:38.500
I got it!

00:55:38.830 --> 00:55:40.620
I know who the culprit is!

00:55:41.080 --> 00:55:41.880
Dad?

00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:42.330
Who?

00:55:42.330 --> 00:55:42.750
Who? Who?

00:55:42.750 --> 00:55:43.340
Who? Who? Who's the culprit?

00:55:45.210 --> 00:55:51.590
The deceased Juri-san only consumed two
types of things after boarding this plane.

00:55:52.140 --> 00:55:53.390
Those two types of things were ...

00:55:53.970 --> 00:55:56.430
The chocolates we were just discussing, and ...

00:55:56.850 --> 00:55:58.390
Tenko-san's vitamin pills.

00:56:00.020 --> 00:56:00.890
You?

00:56:01.480 --> 00:56:03.060
You understand now, right?

00:56:03.980 --> 00:56:08.230
The culprit who killed Maki Juri-san on this plane is ...

00:56:13.320 --> 00:56:15.530
Tenko-san, it's you!

00:56:17.830 --> 00:56:19.500
Don't joke around!

00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:20.910
A false accusation is a serious matter!

00:56:20.910 --> 00:56:23.120
In the first place, I don't even have a motive!

00:56:23.120 --> 00:56:24.000
Is that so, I wonder?

00:56:25.340 --> 00:56:29.800
There's no one here who doesn't have a motive to kill Juri-san, is there?

00:56:32.130 --> 00:56:33.840
What are you talking about?

00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:37.310
You're the hair dresser and make-up artist Sakai Natsuki-san, right?

00:56:37.890 --> 00:56:39.100
If you could explain.

00:56:41.520 --> 00:56:45.310
I have been with Juri-san for a long time ...

00:56:45.310 --> 00:56:49.070
So I believe I'm the one most familiar with her relationships with others.

00:56:49.570 --> 00:56:50.740
First, Ban-san ...

00:56:51.900 --> 00:56:55.120
Although he held the title of play director ...

00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:58.990
In reality, it had been Juri-san, the
chairman, doing all the directing.

00:57:02.580 --> 00:57:06.380
Originally, it was he who trained Juri-san to become an actress, but ...

00:57:06.960 --> 00:57:08.670
It all reversed.

00:57:08.670 --> 00:57:10.670
He couldn't even oppose her.

00:57:11.340 --> 00:57:17.050
I've seen him getting angrily told off by his
wife, Tenko-san, over this matter many times.

00:57:20.060 --> 00:57:24.480
Narusawa-san was asked for a divorce by
Juri-san three years ago and agreed, but ...

00:57:24.850 --> 00:57:27.060
It seems he still has feelings for her.

00:57:27.610 --> 00:57:30.730
No matter how many times he begged
her for reconciliation, he was rejected.

00:57:33.860 --> 00:57:38.450
She also seemed to be getting bored with her young lover, Shinjou-san ...

00:57:38.450 --> 00:57:41.830
And asked me to introduce some other cute guys to her.

00:57:43.200 --> 00:57:45.620
Then there's her manager, Masayo-san.

00:57:46.580 --> 00:57:50.590
Juri-san has always criticized her as dull and dim-witted ...

00:57:50.590 --> 00:57:53.050
Often humiliating her in front of everyone.

00:57:54.220 --> 00:57:55.930
And then there's myself.

00:57:55.930 --> 00:57:58.340
I was always being abused by the selfish Juri-san.

00:57:59.100 --> 00:58:03.020
When I wanted to get another job, she interfered.

00:58:03.020 --> 00:58:05.190
I pretended nothing was wrong, but I resented her.

00:58:06.190 --> 00:58:07.100
See?

00:58:07.100 --> 00:58:09.770
That's why it wouldn't be strange at all if any one of us murdered her.

00:58:12.780 --> 00:58:14.570
Hey, Genta-kun ...

00:58:14.570 --> 00:58:17.030
How can you eat at a time like this?

00:58:17.030 --> 00:58:19.490
Because it'd all go to waste otherwise.

00:58:21.950 --> 00:58:23.080
Delicious!

00:58:29.650 --> 00:58:31.900
If the poison had been on her fingers ...

00:58:32.900 --> 00:58:35.530
The first person to have touched her hand was Shinjou-san.

00:58:36.450 --> 00:58:38.200
Could he has placed the poison at that time?

00:58:39.530 --> 00:58:40.160
No.

00:58:40.410 --> 00:58:41.280
There were other opportunities.

00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:45.040
What if the poison was on the signature pen?

00:58:46.660 --> 00:58:49.790
Maybe the poison was placed on the switch for the reading light.

00:58:50.420 --> 00:58:51.340
No, also ...

00:58:52.210 --> 00:58:55.050
Poison could have been applied to areas in the
restroom Juri-san would have been likely to touch ...

00:58:58.090 --> 00:59:02.680
That's right—after Juri-san went into the
lavatory, she came out rather quickly.

00:59:04.060 --> 00:59:05.390
Wait a minute, before that!

00:59:10.480 --> 00:59:11.440
I see!

00:59:12.400 --> 00:59:13.610
So that's how it was!

00:59:13.980 --> 00:59:14.980
That's why she ...

00:59:15.820 --> 00:59:17.530
For some reason, I'm not feeling too well.

00:59:18.570 --> 00:59:20.410
I've figured out this trick ...

00:59:20.910 --> 00:59:23.080
And the culprit who set it up!

00:59:31.560 --> 00:59:33.230
Ah-le-le, Uncle!

00:59:33.860 --> 00:59:35.280
What do you think that is?

00:59:35.280 --> 00:59:36.110
What?

00:59:36.650 --> 00:59:37.570
There's nothing there.

00:59:38.650 --> 00:59:39.150
What?

00:59:41.140 --> 00:59:42.220
All right, and now!

00:59:47.640 --> 00:59:48.100
Damn it!

00:59:52.500 --> 00:59:54.090
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:59:55.130 --> 00:59:56.840
I guess I was just seeing things!

00:59:56.840 --> 00:59:58.050
I'm going to the restroom!

00:59:58.880 --> 01:00:00.050
What's with him?

01:00:01.990 --> 01:00:03.240
No choice ...

01:00:03.240 --> 01:00:04.330
This will be the first time, though ...

01:00:05.850 --> 01:00:08.060
Dear, you can stop putting on airs.

01:00:08.770 --> 01:00:09.430
Wha—?

01:00:09.710 --> 01:00:10.290
Oh, no!

01:00:10.290 --> 01:00:10.870
I messed up!

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:12.020
Sonoko?

01:00:12.020 --> 01:00:12.850
Me?

01:00:13.610 --> 01:00:15.110
That's quite enough.

01:00:15.110 --> 01:00:16.820
Let's hear the truth from you.

01:00:17.230 --> 01:00:18.320
What?

01:00:18.320 --> 01:00:22.280
Well, it's not like this case is of a caliber
that requires Sleeping Kogorou to solve it.

01:00:22.820 --> 01:00:25.740
All right, I'll explain the situation.

01:00:26.780 --> 01:00:27.450
No way ...

01:00:27.450 --> 01:00:28.450
All right!

01:00:28.450 --> 01:00:30.620
Today it's Auntie's Deduction Show!

01:00:31.250 --> 01:00:34.830
We'll begin with the method the culprit used to administer the poison.

01:00:35.540 --> 01:00:39.460
From that altogether unsurprising modus operandi ...

01:00:41.420 --> 01:00:43.550
And that would be ear clearing.

01:00:44.010 --> 01:00:45.390
Ear clearing?

01:00:46.100 --> 01:00:48.260
Once Juri-san boarded the aircraft ...

01:00:48.260 --> 01:00:50.060
She would definitely have to clear her ears.

01:00:50.520 --> 01:00:51.640
The culprit knew this.

01:00:52.480 --> 01:00:56.480
They knew that she would use the method in which she'd pinch
her nose with her thumb and forefinger while she blew ...

01:00:57.070 --> 01:00:59.070
And that she always used her right hand in doing so.

01:01:00.320 --> 01:01:06.120
Perhaps some of those present are aware that this method
of ear clearing is among the first things taught to new divers.

01:01:06.780 --> 01:01:10.660
After becoming an advanced diver, it's possible to
clear your ears without pinching your nose, but ...

01:01:10.660 --> 01:01:12.830
Juri-san was still a beginner.

01:01:12.830 --> 01:01:14.750
Nine times out of ten, she would have done it.

01:01:15.960 --> 01:01:16.920
Isn't that right, dear?

01:01:18.670 --> 01:01:19.300
Yeah ...

01:01:20.050 --> 01:01:21.130
Hold on!

01:01:21.130 --> 01:01:22.550
How'd you know that?

01:01:23.420 --> 01:01:24.050
Uhm ...

01:01:24.050 --> 01:01:25.300
This method of ear clearing ...

01:01:25.300 --> 01:01:26.800
Similar to how Ayumi-chan felt ...

01:01:27.550 --> 01:01:30.970
It's somewhat embarrassing for a female to do
so in front someone of the opposite gender ...

01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:35.770
Not to mention that Juri-san was an
actress and you were sitting next to her.

01:01:36.310 --> 01:01:38.860
No matter how much of a blockhead you
are, you are of the opposite gender ...

01:01:39.480 --> 01:01:40.360
Blockhead!?

01:01:40.900 --> 01:01:45.660
That was why Juri-san went to the
lavatory to clear her ears in private.

01:01:45.990 --> 01:01:52.120
Then, upon returning to her seat, she used the thumb and
forefinger of her right hand to pick up the chocolate and eat it.

01:01:52.660 --> 01:01:55.790
As had happened many times before, she even
licked the cocoa powder that got on her fingers.

01:01:57.000 --> 01:02:04.380
She was unaware this habit of hers was being exploited in
order to complete the introduction of poison into her body.

01:02:06.800 --> 01:02:08.340
What do you mean?

01:02:08.340 --> 01:02:09.510
Where exactly was the poison?

01:02:13.600 --> 01:02:16.020
It feels like it's kind of hard to breathe, doesn't it?

01:02:16.690 --> 01:02:17.310
Yeah.

01:02:17.650 --> 01:02:18.650
Weird, isn't it?

01:02:20.900 --> 01:02:26.070
Actually, the poison was already slowly entering Juri-san's body.

01:02:27.110 --> 01:02:30.530
Right, the reason she wasn't feeling well ...

01:02:30.530 --> 01:02:33.080
Was because of the poison that was being absorbed through her skin.

01:02:33.450 --> 01:02:34.330
Her skin?

01:02:35.500 --> 01:02:36.410
If that's the case, could it be ...

01:02:36.890 --> 01:02:37.350
Yes.

01:02:38.460 --> 01:02:41.380
Inside the car parked in the lot at Haneda Airport ...

01:02:42.050 --> 01:02:45.670
Having applied the poison and foundation
mixture to both sides of Juri-san's nose ...

01:02:46.880 --> 01:02:49.180
The culprit responsible for Juri-san's death ...

01:02:50.140 --> 01:02:52.100
You, Sakai Natsuki-san ...

01:02:52.890 --> 01:02:53.770
It was you!

01:03:02.820 --> 01:03:04.440
That's not possible!

01:03:04.440 --> 01:03:06.690
Still, that was a fairly interesting deduction!

01:03:08.200 --> 01:03:09.780
Conan-kun mentioned it to me ...

01:03:10.660 --> 01:03:15.040
That you scolded the children who were playing with the foundation.

01:03:16.620 --> 01:03:19.290
It was as a precaution against the one in a million chance ...

01:03:19.290 --> 01:03:25.590
That they would mess with it on the day you
would use it to commit the murder, wasn't it?

01:03:26.920 --> 01:03:29.880
Then, if you're so sure, show me your evidence!

01:03:30.470 --> 01:03:31.590
That's right ...

01:03:31.590 --> 01:03:34.850
If we had examined the thumb and forefinger of Juri-san's right hand ...

01:03:34.850 --> 01:03:40.100
And actually found poison-laced foundation there,
it would have served as sufficient evidence, but ...

01:03:40.600 --> 01:03:45.270
Given that Juri-san licked the poison off,
that evidence has vanished, hasn't it?

01:03:46.900 --> 01:03:49.110
But, there is other evidence.

01:03:50.150 --> 01:03:53.030
The bottle of poisoned foundation and the sponge.

01:03:53.990 --> 01:03:57.450
Smart as you are, you wouldn't have brought those two items aboard.

01:03:58.200 --> 01:04:02.330
On the other hand, disposing of them in the airport
trash cans would have likewise been dangerous.

01:04:03.250 --> 01:04:04.290
Right.

01:04:04.290 --> 01:04:06.050
If it were me, I would have sent it ...

01:04:06.880 --> 01:04:09.340
Addressed back to my own house, via the mail.

01:04:11.180 --> 01:04:16.680
Well, if we contact the airport post office and have
them investigate the mail parcel, we'll know for sure.

01:04:17.640 --> 01:04:20.060
Well, would you care to tell us?

01:04:20.560 --> 01:04:22.350
Your home address.

01:04:38.870 --> 01:04:39.870
That woman ...

01:04:40.500 --> 01:04:42.330
She destroyed my dream.

01:04:43.750 --> 01:04:44.330
Your dream?

01:04:45.960 --> 01:04:50.670
It had been my dream to become a Hollywood make-up artist.

01:04:52.800 --> 01:04:57.140
In order to fulfill my dream, I studied abroad
at a make-up school in Los Angeles ...

01:04:57.560 --> 01:04:59.220
And even mastered speaking conversational English.

01:05:00.770 --> 01:05:05.230
Upon my return to Japan, while helping this
woman with her hairstyling and make-up ...

01:05:05.230 --> 01:05:07.610
I continued to write to Hollywood seeking employment.

01:05:08.730 --> 01:05:12.950
Then, one month ago, when a Hollywood actress came to Japan ...

01:05:13.530 --> 01:05:19.490
An agent who recognized my make-up skill
approached me asking if I wanted to work with her.

01:05:20.700 --> 01:05:24.370
To me, it was the chance of a lifetime.

01:05:25.290 --> 01:05:26.000
But ...

01:05:27.500 --> 01:05:28.960
But that woman ...

01:05:28.960 --> 01:05:31.210
That woman secretly intervened and destroyed that opportunity.

01:05:32.510 --> 01:05:34.760
She really didn't want to let you go.

01:05:34.970 --> 01:05:38.970
I could have forgiven her if she had done it because
she needed me because of my make-up skills!

01:05:40.640 --> 01:05:42.060
But that wasn't it ...

01:05:43.020 --> 01:05:47.770
She had only wanted me by her side in order
to use me as a servant to her many whims.

01:05:50.230 --> 01:05:54.030
After I found out everything, I realized l
had no choice but to go through with it ...

01:05:54.860 --> 01:05:58.950
She'd ruined my pride as a make-up artist.

01:06:02.580 --> 01:06:04.790
Your pride as a make-up artist?

01:06:05.580 --> 01:06:06.620
Don't make me laugh!

01:06:08.290 --> 01:06:11.750
If that were the case, why would you use your make-up as a weapon?

01:06:13.800 --> 01:06:17.840
At this moment, you have no right to talk about pride.

01:06:21.200 --> 01:06:21.910
I ...

01:06:23.250 --> 01:06:24.080
I ...

01:06:26.560 --> 01:06:28.560
You're still young.

01:06:28.560 --> 01:06:31.940
After you've repaid your debt to society, you can start over.

01:06:43.930 --> 01:06:46.560
What is this, this feeling of dread?

01:06:47.940 --> 01:06:49.730
It's like the inside of my head is tingling ...

01:06:55.280 --> 01:06:55.950
This is bad!

01:06:56.470 --> 01:06:57.380
Hey!

01:06:57.380 --> 01:07:00.550
Tell the captain and co-pilot not to eat the snacks you just gave them!

01:07:01.760 --> 01:07:04.020
If you don't hurry, the captain and co-pilot will be in danger!

01:07:04.310 --> 01:07:05.850
You're stupid, aren't you?

01:07:05.850 --> 01:07:07.560
There's no poison in the snacks.

01:07:07.810 --> 01:07:08.730
It's not the snacks!

01:07:08.730 --> 01:07:11.770
It's their fingers that could have poison on them!

01:07:12.270 --> 01:07:13.230
What!?

01:07:13.480 --> 01:07:14.400
What's going on here?

01:07:14.400 --> 01:07:15.900
Explain yourself!

01:07:16.400 --> 01:07:17.780
Yes, I'll be right there!

01:07:21.160 --> 01:07:22.120
Sorry for the intrusion.

01:07:24.180 --> 01:07:24.970
As I feared!

01:07:25.540 --> 01:07:26.370
Captain!?

01:07:27.160 --> 01:07:29.120
Captain, what's wrong!?

01:07:29.120 --> 01:07:30.040
Are you all right!?

01:07:30.620 --> 01:07:31.790
What's going on?

01:07:31.790 --> 01:07:32.750
Nakaya-san!

01:07:33.170 --> 01:07:34.130
Are you all right!?

01:07:34.130 --> 01:07:34.920
Captain!

01:07:39.930 --> 01:07:42.390
No, the auto-pilot's been disengaged!

01:07:53.690 --> 01:07:55.440
Captain, please pull yourself together!

01:07:55.440 --> 01:07:56.110
Captain!

01:07:56.110 --> 01:07:57.190
Hurry, pull him up!

01:07:57.190 --> 01:07:57.990
Move the seat out of the way!

01:08:02.620 --> 01:08:03.280
Captain!

01:08:20.110 --> 01:08:21.780
All right, now for the auto-pilot switch ...

01:08:23.760 --> 01:08:24.970
Shinjou-san?

01:08:24.970 --> 01:08:26.180
Not bad, kid.

01:08:26.930 --> 01:08:28.140
Everything's all right now.

01:08:28.140 --> 01:08:29.180
Summon a doctor immediately.

01:08:29.180 --> 01:08:29.560
Got it!

01:08:30.870 --> 01:08:33.500
We are currently experiencing a medical emergency onboard.

01:08:34.380 --> 01:08:38.710
If there is a doctor among the passengers, please identify
yourself to the nearest flight attendant immediately.

01:08:48.040 --> 01:08:51.540
As suspected, they've been poisoned by a fast-acting poison.

01:08:51.540 --> 01:08:54.790
I'll begin administering first-aid if you would
please move them into the passenger cabin.

01:08:55.080 --> 01:08:56.090
All right.

01:08:56.090 --> 01:08:58.130
Narusawa-san, Ban-san—give us a hand!

01:08:58.460 --> 01:08:59.050
Yes, sir!

01:09:00.260 --> 01:09:01.170
The medical kit!

01:09:01.670 --> 01:09:02.090
Yes, ma'am!

01:09:04.090 --> 01:09:05.430
Say, Conan-kun ...

01:09:05.430 --> 01:09:07.140
Why did the captain and co-pilot also ...

01:09:07.510 --> 01:09:10.770
Earlier, Juri-san entered the cockpit.

01:09:10.770 --> 01:09:15.810
At that time, the captain and co-pilot took Juri-san's hand and kissed it.

01:09:16.060 --> 01:09:20.030
I see, so that's when the poison that was on Juri-san's fingers ...

01:09:20.820 --> 01:09:22.450
How unfortunate, then.

01:09:22.900 --> 01:09:28.700
If they had just shaken hands normally, the poison would have
only gotten onto their palms, and they wouldn't have ingested it.

01:09:32.500 --> 01:09:33.660
Whoa ...

01:09:44.090 --> 01:09:45.760
How are they, Doctor?

01:09:45.760 --> 01:09:50.760
Fortunately, they only ingested a very small amount
of the poison, so their lives are not in danger.

01:09:51.520 --> 01:09:52.430
However ...

01:09:52.430 --> 01:09:56.690
They remain in a fuzzy state of consciousness
and will be unable to operate the plane.

01:10:02.030 --> 01:10:03.320
What'd you say!?

01:10:03.320 --> 01:10:05.360
The captain and the co-pilot are unconscious?

01:10:06.780 --> 01:10:07.820
Excuse me ...

01:10:07.820 --> 01:10:08.870
Could I have your name?

01:10:09.470 --> 01:10:11.010
I'm a passenger, my name is Shinjou.

01:10:11.580 --> 01:10:15.370
Shinjou-san, do you know the current flight situation?

01:10:15.690 --> 01:10:17.730
The current altitude is 12000 feet.

01:10:18.270 --> 01:10:19.900
Current speed is 280 knots.

01:10:20.610 --> 01:10:23.530
Fortunately, the ILS for landing has already been inputted ...

01:10:24.110 --> 01:10:27.610
And I have some experience operating the flaps and gears, so I can do it.

01:10:27.950 --> 01:10:30.240
All I need are instructions with regards to the timing.

01:10:30.760 --> 01:10:31.600
Got it.

01:10:31.970 --> 01:10:34.680
We will clear all other landings and takeoffs.

01:10:34.680 --> 01:10:37.810
We'll also put in an immediate request
for a flight captain to come to the tower.

01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:42.300
The current weather around Hakodate is not stable.

01:10:42.300 --> 01:10:47.220
Consequently, all incoming and outbound flights
have been suspended until further notice.

01:10:48.050 --> 01:10:49.970
We appreciate your patience during this time.

01:10:50.470 --> 01:10:51.930
Ladies and gentlemen ...

01:10:52.910 --> 01:10:53.910
So that's that.

01:10:54.410 --> 01:10:56.040
I'll take over the captain's seat.

01:10:57.000 --> 01:10:58.420
As for the co-pilot's seat ...

01:10:59.040 --> 01:10:59.380
Right ...

01:10:59.830 --> 01:11:01.040
Could I get you to take care of it?

01:11:02.960 --> 01:11:06.220
Your judgment with the control yoke earlier was pretty impressive.

01:11:07.650 --> 01:11:08.570
Yay!

01:11:09.720 --> 01:11:12.850
I've flown planes lots of times in the arcade center!

01:11:14.180 --> 01:11:14.770
Hey!

01:11:15.060 --> 01:11:16.810
Conan-kun, no fair!

01:11:16.810 --> 01:11:18.560
I wanna sit there too!

01:11:18.560 --> 01:11:19.480
Me too!

01:11:19.810 --> 01:11:21.060
This isn't a game!

01:11:22.690 --> 01:11:25.650
Also, I won't need anyone to steer anymore.

01:11:26.610 --> 01:11:31.370
It's just that, even with ILS, I'll need to do a
number of things at once during the landing.

01:11:31.370 --> 01:11:33.490
That's the only time I'll have him assist.

01:11:33.870 --> 01:11:35.740
Even so, why that brat?

01:11:36.330 --> 01:11:38.080
At any rate, just leave it to me.

01:11:38.580 --> 01:11:41.540
We'll be landing in around 15 minutes or so.

01:11:41.540 --> 01:11:43.250
Everyone, please return to the passenger cabin.

01:11:48.470 --> 01:11:52.140
Shinjou-kun just said he had some experience, but ...

01:11:52.140 --> 01:11:54.310
Maybe he's got a license to fly a Cessna or something ...

01:11:55.060 --> 01:11:55.560
Huh?

01:11:56.350 --> 01:11:58.890
Dad, Mom seems to be fast asleep.

01:12:00.350 --> 01:12:01.480
What?

01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:07.010
Everyone, please hurry back to your
seats and fasten your seatbelts tightly.

01:12:07.050 --> 01:12:08.420
Everyone, please hurry back to your
seats and fasten your seatbelts tightly.

01:12:10.360 --> 01:12:12.990
Dad, sit next to Mom, all right?

01:12:13.370 --> 01:12:14.490
Geez ...

01:12:14.490 --> 01:12:15.580
Guess it can't be helped.

01:12:22.540 --> 01:12:23.790
Hey, wake up!

01:12:24.750 --> 01:12:25.380
Hey!

01:12:27.130 --> 01:12:27.840
Geez ...

01:12:40.980 --> 01:12:42.270
You're Kid, right?

01:12:43.230 --> 01:12:44.060
What are you talking about?

01:12:44.270 --> 01:12:46.900
Don't be stupid, drop the act.

01:12:46.900 --> 01:12:51.280
In what world would there exist someone who'd let an
elementary school student take the co-pilot's seat?

01:12:52.320 --> 01:12:53.110
You got me there.

01:12:53.910 --> 01:12:55.910
As for the real Shinjou, right now ...

01:12:56.410 --> 01:13:00.000
He's dressed up as a fake Kid and at Juri-san's villa in Hakodate ...

01:13:00.330 --> 01:13:00.790
Right?

01:13:02.750 --> 01:13:06.000
When you got on the plane, Juri-san was angry, you see ...

01:13:06.460 --> 01:13:11.010
I'm pretty sure he was told by Juri-san to be
a fake Kid as entertainment for the party.

01:13:11.380 --> 01:13:12.470
I expected as much from you.

01:13:12.470 --> 01:13:12.970
Except ...

01:13:13.470 --> 01:13:18.430
There's a certain other person who, disbelieving Kid would
give up just like that, had headed to Hakodate as well, so ...

01:13:19.100 --> 01:13:22.980
That person might be chasing after the fake Kid as we speak.

01:13:41.830 --> 01:13:42.620
And?

01:13:42.620 --> 01:13:45.210
When is it you plan on taking possession of the ''Jewel of Destiny''?

01:13:46.290 --> 01:13:47.000
I'm not after it anymore.

01:13:48.790 --> 01:13:50.590
You should know about it as well ...

01:13:50.590 --> 01:13:54.680
A real star sapphire is cold when you touch it with your lips.

01:13:54.680 --> 01:13:55.930
That one's a fake.

01:13:57.990 --> 01:14:01.040
What he did back then—it was to ascertain that!

01:14:03.930 --> 01:14:07.060
It was probably in order to attract playgoers to see <i>Joséphine</i> ...

01:14:07.060 --> 01:14:11.070
That they tried to publicize that fake as the real thing.

01:14:11.570 --> 01:14:12.280
What're you gonna do?

01:14:12.820 --> 01:14:14.280
You gonna arrest me?

01:14:14.280 --> 01:14:15.150
Detective-kun.

01:14:15.780 --> 01:14:20.240
Of course, after this giant metal bird has returned to its nest.

01:14:21.410 --> 01:14:23.120
Sky-J Flight 865.

01:14:23.540 --> 01:14:25.710
Hakodate Tower will now take over.

01:14:26.330 --> 01:14:29.500
Please change the radio frequency to 118.35.

01:14:30.090 --> 01:14:32.000
118.35, roger that.

01:14:34.800 --> 01:14:36.050
This is Hakodate Tower.

01:14:36.340 --> 01:14:38.010
I am the control chief, Uesugi.

01:14:38.510 --> 01:14:40.430
I'll hand you over to Captain Shimaoka.

01:14:41.140 --> 01:14:42.060
This is Shimaoka.

01:14:42.510 --> 01:14:44.430
We'll get right to it—do you see the M.C.P.?

01:14:44.430 --> 01:14:46.580
That's the Mode Control Panel.

01:14:46.620 --> 01:14:47.540
Yes, I see it.

01:14:48.190 --> 01:14:51.650
Then please press the APP button on that panel.

01:14:52.320 --> 01:14:55.530
This will enable the plane to lower itself onto the runway automatically.

01:14:55.940 --> 01:14:56.530
Roger.

01:14:57.110 --> 01:14:58.360
APP ...

01:14:58.780 --> 01:14:59.280
That one.

01:15:01.370 --> 01:15:02.030
It's pressed!

01:15:03.080 --> 01:15:03.990
Who are you?

01:15:04.310 --> 01:15:07.190
I'm Edogawa Conan, Shinjou-san's assistant!

01:15:07.750 --> 01:15:08.670
Assistant?

01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:10.210
Do you have a child next to you?

01:15:10.940 --> 01:15:14.650
Little boy, do not touch the control yoke or any of the other switches!

01:15:14.900 --> 01:15:15.440
Understand?

01:15:17.220 --> 01:15:18.630
Now we can relax for the moment.

01:15:19.180 --> 01:15:21.760
Can you handle operating the flaps and the landing gear?

01:15:22.180 --> 01:15:23.060
Yeah, I got it.

01:15:23.680 --> 01:15:27.520
My father taught me how to pilot a Cessna in Hawaii.

01:15:27.730 --> 01:15:31.230
I see, guess I didn't pick the wrong person for the job after all.

01:15:31.650 --> 01:15:34.400
But, that was all with feet planted firmly on the ground.

01:15:34.980 --> 01:15:37.280
I've never flown for real.

01:15:41.200 --> 01:15:44.830
It's the worst possible weather, but they
should still somehow be able to land, right?

01:15:44.830 --> 01:15:45.200
Yeah.

01:16:04.010 --> 01:16:05.310
Really bad rain ...

01:16:05.310 --> 01:16:06.720
The wind seems pretty strong as well.

01:16:07.270 --> 01:16:09.770
Don't fall, airplane!

01:16:22.030 --> 01:16:22.950
There's the airport!

01:16:28.370 --> 01:16:29.500
Here it comes!

01:16:29.750 --> 01:16:32.120
Flight 865: Flaps to 1.

01:16:36.840 --> 01:16:37.710
Flaps to 5.

01:16:40.280 --> 01:16:41.320
Flaps to 10.

01:16:43.990 --> 01:16:45.990
Lower the wheels, flaps to 20.

01:16:56.980 --> 01:16:58.980
We're finally about to land.

01:17:19.190 --> 01:17:19.650
What the—!?

01:17:20.300 --> 01:17:21.300
It's the lightning!

01:17:21.300 --> 01:17:22.760
We've been struck by lightning!

01:17:23.220 --> 01:17:24.550
This is Flight 865!

01:17:25.390 --> 01:17:27.680
We've just been struck by lightning and all the displays have turned off!

01:17:28.010 --> 01:17:28.930
Calm down.

01:17:28.930 --> 01:17:31.640
Turn the white knob next to the glare shield.

01:17:35.060 --> 01:17:35.940
They're back ...

01:17:35.940 --> 01:17:36.480
Not yet!

01:17:37.610 --> 01:17:39.190
The auto-pilot's not engaged!

01:17:41.490 --> 01:17:42.400
What'd you say!?

01:17:42.720 --> 01:17:44.090
Abort the landing!

01:17:44.090 --> 01:17:46.340
Full thrust and pull up on the control yoke!

01:17:54.500 --> 01:17:56.420
All right, retract the wheels.

01:17:58.880 --> 01:17:59.570
They're retracted!

01:17:59.610 --> 01:18:00.940
Good, now contunue to climb!

01:18:03.610 --> 01:18:04.360
No!

01:18:04.360 --> 01:18:05.490
The wind is blowing it off course!

01:18:05.800 --> 01:18:07.010
Turn to the right!

01:18:07.010 --> 01:18:08.050
Turn right!

01:18:12.100 --> 01:18:14.020
It's going to go right into the terminal building!

01:18:14.020 --> 01:18:15.140
Bring up the nose of the airplane!

01:18:25.950 --> 01:18:27.030
Not good!

01:18:51.930 --> 01:18:52.930
Wow!

01:18:53.680 --> 01:18:55.140
Awesome!

01:18:58.810 --> 01:19:00.020
How's the airport?

01:19:00.020 --> 01:19:01.400
Is the control tower all right?

01:19:02.090 --> 01:19:03.880
Flight 865, can you hear me?

01:19:04.780 --> 01:19:05.440
I can hear you!

01:19:06.150 --> 01:19:06.990
What's the damage assessment?

01:19:07.380 --> 01:19:09.760
No injuries at the tower.

01:19:09.760 --> 01:19:11.470
But the runways can't be used for the time being.

01:19:11.470 --> 01:19:12.140
How's the situation on your side?

01:19:12.780 --> 01:19:14.540
We've lost Engine #2.

01:19:15.310 --> 01:19:16.390
It's all right.

01:19:16.390 --> 01:19:18.940
The remaining three engines are enough to make a landing.

01:19:18.940 --> 01:19:20.440
But keep an eye on your balance.

01:19:20.860 --> 01:19:22.320
The plane is currently stabilized.

01:19:22.320 --> 01:19:24.900
We've just adjusted the rudder, and cut
the throttle down to position three.

01:19:25.170 --> 01:19:27.300
Good, what's your current altitude and speed?

01:19:28.030 --> 01:19:29.530
3000 feet, 200 knots.

01:19:30.430 --> 01:19:33.260
Set the flaps to 5 and level out.

01:19:38.120 --> 01:19:42.590
Turn the nose to 180 degrees and ascend to 4500 feet.

01:19:42.610 --> 01:19:43.150
Roger that.

01:19:44.150 --> 01:19:45.980
All we have to do now is circle around and wait for clearance, then.

01:19:46.440 --> 01:19:47.240
Yeah.

01:19:47.240 --> 01:19:50.990
As long as the auto-pilot functions are restored,
once the runway becomes operable again ...

01:19:51.620 --> 01:19:54.660
We can try landing again using the ILS.

01:19:55.240 --> 01:19:56.330
This is ridiculous!

01:19:56.330 --> 01:19:58.410
Didn't I tell you there aren't enough fire trucks! ?

01:20:03.590 --> 01:20:05.340
You have to put out the blaze on the runway!

01:20:11.640 --> 01:20:12.800
Conan-kun, it's bad!

01:20:12.800 --> 01:20:13.600
It's bad!

01:20:13.890 --> 01:20:15.970
One of the engines fell off!

01:20:15.970 --> 01:20:17.560
We already know, don't worry.

01:20:17.930 --> 01:20:21.480
We can still land safely using three engines that are left.

01:20:21.980 --> 01:20:23.400
And we still have plenty of ...

01:20:24.440 --> 01:20:25.190
What's wrong?

01:20:25.610 --> 01:20:27.110
We're almost out of fuel!

01:20:27.110 --> 01:20:27.650
What?

01:20:29.610 --> 01:20:31.320
Out of fuel!?

01:20:31.950 --> 01:20:33.280
You said we're out of fuel?

01:20:33.280 --> 01:20:34.870
How did that happen!?

01:20:35.410 --> 01:20:37.660
Could it be because the engine fell off?

01:20:38.040 --> 01:20:43.080
No, usually each of the four engines have their own fuel tank, so ...

01:20:43.750 --> 01:20:45.290
The cross-feed valve is open!?

01:20:46.800 --> 01:20:49.630
Hey, what is that cross-something?

01:20:49.630 --> 01:20:50.510
It's a cross-feed valve.

01:20:52.300 --> 01:20:56.680
Pressing that switch opens the valves that separate the tanks ...

01:20:56.680 --> 01:20:58.180
Making it all one big tank.

01:20:58.890 --> 01:21:00.560
Damn, just how did that happen?

01:21:04.290 --> 01:21:04.750
Whoa ...

01:21:06.520 --> 01:21:08.570
Geez, that old geezer.

01:21:08.570 --> 01:21:10.440
That being the case, we don't have a moment to spare.

01:21:10.740 --> 01:21:11.610
Yeah.

01:21:11.610 --> 01:21:14.610
There should be maps over there, someone bring them over.

01:21:11.630 --> 01:21:15.970
Hakodate Tower, this is Flight 865, mayday, mayday!

01:21:16.450 --> 01:21:17.700
Tower, do you copy?

01:21:17.700 --> 01:21:18.700
Please respond!

01:21:18.680 --> 01:21:23.060
Flight 865 ... Hakodate Tower ... please say again ... louder!

01:21:23.080 --> 01:21:23.830
Hey ...

01:21:23.830 --> 01:21:26.000
There's too much static, I can't make them out.

01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:27.710
Exactly what's happened?

01:21:27.710 --> 01:21:28.670
Professor!

01:21:28.670 --> 01:21:31.920
We've lost an engine and the fuel is running low!

01:21:32.260 --> 01:21:33.380
What'd you say!?

01:21:33.630 --> 01:21:35.760
Map, map, map ...

01:21:35.760 --> 01:21:37.100
Should be that red one.

01:21:37.640 --> 01:21:38.350
Got it!

01:21:38.720 --> 01:21:39.260
Damn!

01:21:39.850 --> 01:21:42.020
The auto-pilot, the runway, the fuel ...

01:21:42.020 --> 01:21:44.190
And now even the radio comms are gone as well!

01:21:44.940 --> 01:21:46.270
Did you say the auto-pilot is gone!?

01:21:46.270 --> 01:21:48.650
Then, you're piloting manually right now!?

01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:50.730
Conan-kun!

01:21:50.730 --> 01:21:51.690
Here, the map!

01:21:51.690 --> 01:21:52.190
Thank you.

01:21:52.780 --> 01:21:55.110
There's about 3000 pounds of fuel left.

01:21:55.660 --> 01:21:59.580
At 300 Ibs/min, we've only got 10 minutes of flight time left.

01:21:59.910 --> 01:22:03.210
We need to find somewhere to land within that time.

01:22:03.210 --> 01:22:04.870
What do you mean by ''somewhere''?

01:22:05.290 --> 01:22:08.250
There's no way the last runway is going to be cleared in 10 minutes.

01:22:09.340 --> 01:22:10.460
How about Chitose?

01:22:10.460 --> 01:22:12.050
If we go to the New Chitose Airport ...

01:22:12.050 --> 01:22:15.840
It's very possible we'll run out of fuel before we get there.

01:22:16.590 --> 01:22:18.010
What about other airports?

01:22:18.010 --> 01:22:19.470
Aren't there any others around this area?

01:22:19.470 --> 01:22:20.180
There aren't.

01:22:21.350 --> 01:22:25.060
There might be an agricultural takeoff
and landing strip, or a JSDF base, but ...

01:22:26.310 --> 01:22:28.150
The length of the runway wouldn't be long enough.

01:22:29.730 --> 01:22:33.690
If that's so, how about we try landing on a strip of road instead?

01:22:33.690 --> 01:22:36.660
Hokkaido has a lot of wide and straight roads ...

01:22:36.660 --> 01:22:37.280
That's impossible.

01:22:38.490 --> 01:22:41.080
The span between the wheels on this plane is 11 meters.

01:22:41.700 --> 01:22:47.620
All roads spanning 12 or more meters across are required
to have a central divider as well as traffic signboards.

01:22:48.170 --> 01:22:50.630
There would likely be residences and power lines in the vicinity as well.

01:22:50.630 --> 01:22:52.000
Then, how about a field?

01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:52.500
No way.

01:22:53.630 --> 01:22:55.510
The ground would be too soft.

01:22:55.510 --> 01:22:58.130
Rather, it'd be better to try a water landing in the sea nearby ...

01:22:58.130 --> 01:22:59.550
No ...

01:22:59.550 --> 01:23:02.100
The plane could be tossed by the waves and get turned over ...

01:23:06.250 --> 01:23:06.870
Where?

01:23:07.080 --> 01:23:07.750
Where?

01:23:08.790 --> 01:23:11.540
There has to be somewhere we can land ...

01:23:11.860 --> 01:23:15.490
Somewhere long, straight, and clear of obstructions ...

01:23:18.860 --> 01:23:19.780
Hey ...

01:23:19.780 --> 01:23:22.530
If we aren't able to land, what'll happen to us?

01:23:22.990 --> 01:23:24.370
Well then ...

01:23:24.370 --> 01:23:26.330
We would crash ...

01:23:27.620 --> 01:23:29.040
I don't wanna die!

01:23:29.290 --> 01:23:30.290
Hey, Conan-kun ...

01:23:30.290 --> 01:23:31.380
I know a place!

01:23:32.210 --> 01:23:35.090
It's long, straight, and clear of obstructions!

01:23:36.170 --> 01:23:41.180
A little while ago, they showed that place during
a dolphin and whale watching program on TV ...

01:23:42.200 --> 01:23:43.950
Dolphin and whale watching ...

01:23:44.330 --> 01:23:45.160
Muroran, then?

01:23:47.480 --> 01:23:48.270
The piers!

01:23:52.230 --> 01:23:53.570
Nippon Steel Pier ...

01:23:53.860 --> 01:23:54.770
Nakau Pier ...

01:23:55.190 --> 01:23:56.150
Motowanishi Pier ...

01:23:56.530 --> 01:23:57.490
Muroran Pier ...

01:23:58.150 --> 01:23:59.030
Nisseki Pier ...

01:23:59.990 --> 01:24:00.490
Found it!

01:24:00.860 --> 01:24:01.740
Sakimori Pier!

01:24:03.330 --> 01:24:04.160
Its length ...

01:24:04.910 --> 01:24:06.750
Approximately 1400 meters ...

01:24:06.750 --> 01:24:09.290
Its width is probably about 30 meters across!

01:24:09.290 --> 01:24:11.330
But the width of this plane is ...

01:24:11.330 --> 01:24:12.210
Yeah ...

01:24:12.210 --> 01:24:13.710
Just short of 60 meters.

01:24:14.040 --> 01:24:17.510
But, if we let one side of the wings hover
over the ocean, we should be able to.

01:24:17.510 --> 01:24:18.510
Impossible.

01:24:18.510 --> 01:24:19.590
That isn't enough stopping distance.

01:24:20.340 --> 01:24:24.510
This plane should need more than 2000 meters of stopping distance.

01:24:25.010 --> 01:24:27.560
The integrity of the ground surface is also a problem ...

01:24:28.180 --> 01:24:32.060
Luckily, or unluckily, there's not much fuel
left and there aren't many passengers.

01:24:32.480 --> 01:24:36.860
The lighter we are, the shorter the stopping distance.

01:24:36.860 --> 01:24:39.320
Depending on the wind direction, it may be even shorter.

01:24:40.650 --> 01:24:42.610
According to the weather report I saw at Haneda Airport ...

01:24:42.610 --> 01:24:45.160
They said strong winds from the west will blow throughout the night!

01:24:45.450 --> 01:24:46.470
Really, Mitsuhiko?

01:24:46.510 --> 01:24:46.930
Yes!

01:24:47.330 --> 01:24:50.290
This pier pretty much stretches east to west.

01:24:50.870 --> 01:24:54.960
As long as we head into the west wind and land
from the east, we may just be able to land!

01:24:54.960 --> 01:24:55.670
It's impossible.

01:24:56.670 --> 01:25:00.590
When we collided with the control tower
earlier, I took a strong blow to my left arm ...

01:25:01.170 --> 01:25:03.800
I've been mostly controlling the plane
using only my right hand ever since ...

01:25:05.180 --> 01:25:07.060
If we're going to land manually ...

01:25:07.930 --> 01:25:10.140
I'll need to hold on to the control yoke tightly with both hands.

01:25:14.940 --> 01:25:16.310
You—how's your vision?

01:25:17.770 --> 01:25:19.150
1.5 in both eyes.

01:25:19.900 --> 01:25:20.860
Any chronic diseases?

01:25:20.860 --> 01:25:23.360
No ...

01:25:23.360 --> 01:25:24.780
And your bust, waist, and hip sizes?

01:25:25.070 --> 01:25:26.950
Let me see, my bust is ...

01:25:28.700 --> 01:25:29.580
What!?

01:25:29.910 --> 01:25:31.450
Good, you've passed.

01:25:32.000 --> 01:25:34.080
Sit here in my place.

01:25:34.670 --> 01:25:36.080
What are you saying!?

01:25:36.080 --> 01:25:37.630
I don't know anything about flying a plane!

01:25:38.130 --> 01:25:39.210
It'll be all right.

01:25:39.210 --> 01:25:41.300
I'll be behind you, teaching you how to work it.

01:25:41.920 --> 01:25:44.430
All you have to do is hold on to the control yoke.

01:25:45.010 --> 01:25:46.680
I can't—there's no way!

01:25:51.640 --> 01:25:52.390
The plane!

01:25:52.850 --> 01:25:54.190
The plane's falling!

01:25:54.190 --> 01:25:55.350
It's gonna crash!

01:25:55.730 --> 01:25:57.310
Ran-neechan, hurry and sit!

01:26:02.650 --> 01:26:05.780
And now, slowly pull the control yoke towards you.

01:26:06.320 --> 01:26:07.280
Steady ...

01:26:13.960 --> 01:26:15.000
Great, nicely done.

01:26:15.580 --> 01:26:16.500
Easy, wasn't it?

01:26:16.500 --> 01:26:17.580
Not at all!

01:26:18.500 --> 01:26:19.790
What direction to Muroran?

01:26:19.790 --> 01:26:20.840
Looking for it right now.

01:26:22.300 --> 01:26:23.050
Found it!

01:26:23.340 --> 01:26:27.390
It just so happens that the Hakodate to
Sapporo flight path passes near Muroran.

01:26:28.970 --> 01:26:30.390
The bearing is 023 degrees.

01:26:30.930 --> 01:26:32.060
023, is it?

01:26:38.770 --> 01:26:40.060
We'll pass over a mountain.

01:26:40.060 --> 01:26:41.570
Our altitude needs to remain over 5000.

01:26:41.570 --> 01:26:42.030
Roger.

01:26:42.820 --> 01:26:43.610
Excuse me ...

01:26:44.190 --> 01:26:46.780
Please tell the passengers we're heading to Chitose.

01:26:46.780 --> 01:26:47.320
Yes, sir.

01:26:47.610 --> 01:26:50.990
Also, please transfer everyone on the second floor downstairs.

01:26:51.990 --> 01:26:54.410
If they discover a high school girl is piloting the plane ...

01:26:54.410 --> 01:26:56.000
They may well panic.

01:26:56.870 --> 01:26:58.790
You guys return to the cabin too.

01:27:01.290 --> 01:27:04.840
Even if you stayed here, there's nothing else you guys can do.

01:27:04.840 --> 01:27:09.760
I'd also like for you guys to keep an eye on the other
children and make sure they don't cause trouble.

01:27:11.300 --> 01:27:13.220
This is a very important job.

01:27:13.850 --> 01:27:15.520
If you can't do it, I'll ask someone else, but ...

01:27:16.060 --> 01:27:17.100
How about it?

01:27:17.100 --> 01:27:17.690
Can you?

01:27:18.190 --> 01:27:19.100
Understood.

01:27:19.100 --> 01:27:20.230
We'll do our best!

01:27:20.230 --> 01:27:21.150
Leave it to us!

01:27:21.900 --> 01:27:22.570
All right!

01:27:22.570 --> 01:27:23.270
I owe you guys!

01:27:23.610 --> 01:27:24.440
Roger!

01:27:27.280 --> 01:27:28.610
I'm staying.

01:27:28.610 --> 01:27:31.820
Because if anything happens, Ran won't
have anyone else that can help her.

01:27:37.830 --> 01:27:38.830
That'll be fine.

01:27:39.420 --> 01:27:43.130
All right, I'll explain the other controls en route ...

01:27:43.130 --> 01:27:44.050
There's not much time left.

01:27:44.840 --> 01:27:45.590
Let's go!

01:27:52.970 --> 01:27:54.680
Flight SKY-J 865!

01:27:55.100 --> 01:27:56.720
This is Hakodate Tower!

01:27:56.720 --> 01:27:58.060
Do you copy?

01:27:58.060 --> 01:27:58.980
Please respond!

01:27:59.770 --> 01:28:03.230
It's no use, they're not even responding on the emergency line.

01:28:03.860 --> 01:28:05.360
Take a look!

01:28:05.360 --> 01:28:07.490
Flight 865 is heading away.

01:28:08.780 --> 01:28:10.530
Where do you suppose they're going?

01:28:22.420 --> 01:28:24.420
So that's the Great Shiratori Bridge, then?

01:28:25.000 --> 01:28:28.010
That's quite impressive, Shiratori-kun!

01:28:28.420 --> 01:28:31.840
Sorry to disappoint, Inspector, but that's the Hakucho Bridge.

01:28:28.610 --> 01:28:32.990
The kanji "白鳥" can be read as either "Hakucho" or "Shiratori"

01:28:32.550 --> 01:28:37.310
Coming to Muroran as you suggested on the way back
from our business trip to Sapporo was well worth it.

01:28:37.540 --> 01:28:40.500
My, the Great Shiratori Bridge sure is beautiful ...

01:28:38.790 --> 01:28:42.270
Hakucho Bridge

01:28:43.000 --> 01:28:45.670
Someday, I'll bring Miwako-san here ...

01:28:48.050 --> 01:28:50.010
This is definitely not on my list.

01:28:57.160 --> 01:28:59.290
That's an amazing number of patrol cars!

01:28:59.950 --> 01:29:02.540
Perhaps they're chasing after a particularly vicious fiend ...

01:29:02.540 --> 01:29:03.370
All right.

01:29:03.370 --> 01:29:04.630
Let's check it out!

01:29:08.190 --> 01:29:10.820
Ladies and gentlemen ...

01:29:10.800 --> 01:29:12.760
I'm scared, Mama!

01:29:10.820 --> 01:29:13.950
There has been a small accident on the plane.

01:29:13.220 --> 01:29:14.510
It's gonna be fine, right?

01:29:13.950 --> 01:29:18.120
We will be diverting to New Chitose Airport.

01:29:18.120 --> 01:29:19.910
It should be a smooth flight.

01:29:19.910 --> 01:29:23.370
We apologize for the inconvenience and thank you for your understanding.

01:29:20.770 --> 01:29:22.310
We're really going to Muroran, right?

01:29:28.860 --> 01:29:30.190
We're approaching Muroran.

01:29:31.070 --> 01:29:33.110
Descend to 2000 feet.

01:29:33.110 --> 01:29:33.530
Yes, sir.

01:29:43.210 --> 01:29:43.920
There!

01:29:43.920 --> 01:29:44.670
I can see the lights!

01:29:45.170 --> 01:29:46.000
That's Muroran Harbor!

01:29:46.710 --> 01:29:48.460
Sakimori Pier is more to the left!

01:29:49.090 --> 01:29:50.380
On the other side of Hakucho Bridge!

01:29:52.240 --> 01:29:52.900
No good!

01:29:55.090 --> 01:29:56.090
Hey ...

01:29:56.430 --> 01:29:58.050
It's dark—I can't see anything.

01:29:58.550 --> 01:30:01.560
Wait, is that really where we're going to land?

01:30:02.160 --> 01:30:02.830
What now?

01:30:03.210 --> 01:30:05.120
We can't turn back now ...

01:30:05.690 --> 01:30:06.730
Hey ...

01:30:06.730 --> 01:30:08.060
Can we do this, Conan-kun?

01:30:15.410 --> 01:30:15.990
What're you—!?

01:30:16.530 --> 01:30:18.910
Looks pretty bad, so I'm bailing.

01:30:19.660 --> 01:30:20.490
Good luck.

01:30:21.240 --> 01:30:22.040
Hold on!

01:30:22.040 --> 01:30:23.080
Hey, wait!

01:30:25.960 --> 01:30:27.540
Ran-neechan, lower the nose of the plane!

01:30:38.590 --> 01:30:39.890
Wait, what do you think you're doing?

01:30:40.680 --> 01:30:41.970
Grab onto something!

01:30:46.810 --> 01:30:47.650
What?

01:30:47.650 --> 01:30:48.310
What happened?

01:30:48.860 --> 01:30:49.560
It's fine.

01:30:49.560 --> 01:30:50.480
Don't worry.

01:30:50.860 --> 01:30:52.530
Just keep the plane steady.

01:30:59.640 --> 01:31:00.180
K-

01:31:00.970 --> 01:31:01.470
K-

01:31:02.580 --> 01:31:03.490
Kaitou Kid!

01:31:05.250 --> 01:31:06.790
Well, young miss ...

01:31:06.790 --> 01:31:11.500
Let us meet again someday, under the pale moonlight.

01:31:12.480 --> 01:31:13.150
Yes.

01:31:13.380 --> 01:31:14.130
Bye!

01:31:26.520 --> 01:31:27.520
He jumped off!?

01:31:27.690 --> 01:31:28.390
That's right!

01:31:28.390 --> 01:31:30.230
Shinjou-san was Kid!

01:31:30.460 --> 01:31:31.380
I see ...

01:31:31.380 --> 01:31:33.340
So that's why he pressed the depressurization button.

01:31:33.690 --> 01:31:36.360
He got scared because we're going to crash, so he fled!

01:31:36.780 --> 01:31:37.610
And I was a fan of his ...

01:31:37.610 --> 01:31:38.320
That jerk!

01:31:38.780 --> 01:31:42.660
Sonoko-neechan, isn't it a bit early to say we're gonna crash?

01:31:42.660 --> 01:31:43.620
But, Conan-kun ...

01:31:45.080 --> 01:31:46.200
What are we going to do now?

01:31:48.120 --> 01:31:51.290
Now it's up to us to land the plane, Ran-neechan.

01:31:53.290 --> 01:31:55.250
I told you it'll be fine, Ran!

01:31:55.460 --> 01:31:58.550
Don't they always say, '’Ask three people
and you'll be wiser than a pearl''?

01:31:58.550 --> 01:31:59.510
We'll pull through somehow!

01:31:59.990 --> 01:32:02.280
Hey, hey, the saying goes ...

01:32:04.310 --> 01:32:06.850
The saying goes, ''Wiser than Mañjuśrī", doesn't it?

01:32:04.620 --> 01:32:08.330
Note: Manjusri is the bodhisattva of transcendent wisdom

01:32:06.850 --> 01:32:07.980
Was that it?

01:32:11.730 --> 01:32:15.270
Anyway, let's circle around the pier and take a closer look!

01:32:21.320 --> 01:32:22.570
Help!

01:32:23.240 --> 01:32:24.780
Please help me!

01:32:25.580 --> 01:32:28.620
I'm not Kid—you've got the wrong guy!

01:32:29.000 --> 01:32:30.790
Then why did you run?

01:32:31.500 --> 01:32:34.000
Because I once stole a clock ...

01:32:34.460 --> 01:32:36.800
See, you are Kid!

01:32:37.170 --> 01:32:38.550
Inspector Nakamori ...

01:32:38.550 --> 01:32:39.050
What?

01:32:39.590 --> 01:32:40.720
What's that over there?

01:32:44.140 --> 01:32:45.640
Isn't it obvious?

01:32:45.640 --> 01:32:46.930
That's Kid.

01:32:48.430 --> 01:32:49.270
Kid!?

01:32:53.730 --> 01:32:54.980
Then, you are ...

01:32:55.310 --> 01:32:57.110
I told you, you've got the wrong guy!

01:33:00.360 --> 01:33:02.150
Sonoko-neechan, how's it look?

01:33:02.910 --> 01:33:03.990
Not good at all.

01:33:03.990 --> 01:33:06.080
There's some lights here and there, but ...

01:33:06.080 --> 01:33:07.870
It's mostly pitch-black and I can't really see anything.

01:33:08.220 --> 01:33:08.930
Damn!

01:33:11.870 --> 01:33:13.460
Are you all right, Ran-neechan?

01:33:14.830 --> 01:33:16.130
What's wrong, Ran?

01:33:16.790 --> 01:33:18.090
I don't know ...

01:33:18.090 --> 01:33:19.670
Just that suddenly, I feel ...

01:33:21.470 --> 01:33:22.340
Conan-kun ...

01:33:23.010 --> 01:33:24.720
I can't do it after all.

01:33:24.720 --> 01:33:25.930
No way!

01:33:25.930 --> 01:33:27.310
You can do it, Ran-neechan!

01:33:28.620 --> 01:33:29.580
This is bad ...

01:33:29.870 --> 01:33:31.210
It'll be too dangerous with her like this.

01:33:32.230 --> 01:33:34.520
Sonoko-neechan, switch with me for a bit.

01:33:34.520 --> 01:33:36.020
I'm going to the restroom.

01:33:36.020 --> 01:33:37.060
The restroom?

01:33:37.190 --> 01:33:38.480
I'll be right back, but ...

01:33:38.480 --> 01:33:42.610
Just in case the radio comes back on,
you should both put on your headsets!

01:33:43.360 --> 01:33:44.160
Wait!

01:33:45.950 --> 01:33:49.120
Geez, going to the restroom at a time like this?

01:33:49.990 --> 01:33:51.160
This is why little brats—

01:33:54.120 --> 01:33:54.710
Hello?

01:33:54.870 --> 01:33:55.710
Hello!?

01:33:56.230 --> 01:33:56.810
Ran.

01:33:57.270 --> 01:33:58.570
Can you hear me, Ran?

01:34:01.460 --> 01:34:02.470
Shinichi?

01:34:03.010 --> 01:34:05.760
I'm calling from the control tower in Sapporo.

01:34:06.590 --> 01:34:09.140
Looks like you guys are in a bit of a mess.

01:34:10.910 --> 01:34:12.830
But everything will be all right.

01:34:12.830 --> 01:34:16.670
Just stay calm, follow my instructions,
and you'll definitely land in one piece.

01:34:18.150 --> 01:34:21.280
I'll protect you at all costs, so don't worry!

01:34:22.800 --> 01:34:23.760
Are you listening, Ran?

01:34:25.990 --> 01:34:27.450
Ran, answer him!

01:34:29.240 --> 01:34:29.990
What is this?

01:34:30.660 --> 01:34:32.160
You're acting all confident ...

01:34:32.910 --> 01:34:34.460
Do you even know?

01:34:34.460 --> 01:34:37.540
That the lives of all the passengers are in my hands!?

01:34:38.000 --> 01:34:39.540
Don't act so nonchalant about it!

01:34:41.460 --> 01:34:43.510
When I really need you, you're never here ...

01:34:43.510 --> 01:34:45.010
All I get is a phone call!

01:34:46.680 --> 01:34:49.510
Even when you finally make it back,
you're gone again in the next instant ...

01:34:54.100 --> 01:34:55.020
Every time ...

01:34:58.020 --> 01:34:58.850
Every single time ...

01:35:03.670 --> 01:35:04.510
No!

01:35:04.510 --> 01:35:05.050
I don't want to hear it!

01:35:05.260 --> 01:35:07.010
Shinichi-niichan said ...

01:35:07.510 --> 01:35:08.720
Wait for me, Ran.

01:35:09.350 --> 01:35:10.720
Don't run away!

01:35:10.720 --> 01:35:12.720
I'll be right back!

01:35:12.910 --> 01:35:14.910
You always leave me behind, all alone ...

01:35:15.560 --> 01:35:18.230
He said that he wants you to wait for him until then.

01:35:19.080 --> 01:35:21.000
What do you take me for!?

01:35:29.280 --> 01:35:30.240
I ...

01:35:40.440 --> 01:35:41.980
I like you ...

01:35:41.980 --> 01:35:43.070
Shinichi.

01:35:49.180 --> 01:35:49.890
Ran ...

01:35:50.470 --> 01:35:51.140
There's light!

01:35:51.970 --> 01:35:52.970
I see light!

01:35:53.660 --> 01:35:55.950
There are red lights moving around like an obi!

01:35:56.200 --> 01:35:56.790
What?

01:36:03.190 --> 01:36:04.780
So that's what's going on ...

01:36:12.050 --> 01:36:13.970
Damn it, that bastard Kid!

01:36:13.970 --> 01:36:14.760
You're not getting away!

01:36:17.310 --> 01:36:18.140
Hey!

01:36:18.140 --> 01:36:19.690
Kid's headed toward the pier!

01:36:19.690 --> 01:36:20.520
Got it.

01:36:21.020 --> 01:36:22.520
Kid is now headed toward the pier.

01:36:22.520 --> 01:36:25.020
A-Team, B-Team, take opposite sides and wrap around.

01:36:25.020 --> 01:36:27.360
Align the patrol cars all along the edges of the pier!

01:36:27.490 --> 01:36:29.820
C-Team, follow my lead!

01:36:29.990 --> 01:36:31.530
We'll attack Kid from all sides!

01:36:38.080 --> 01:36:39.870
Patrol cars coming, Gramps.

01:36:40.210 --> 01:36:42.170
Something must have happened, I guess.

01:36:42.170 --> 01:36:44.000
Looks like they're coming from this side, too.

01:36:55.850 --> 01:36:56.760
Ran!

01:36:56.760 --> 01:36:58.180
Begin landing preparations!

01:36:59.200 --> 01:37:02.460
Those lights are probably the patrol cars that Kid lured there.

01:37:02.900 --> 01:37:05.230
So that's why he jumped off ...

01:37:05.230 --> 01:37:07.980
It was in order to set up a runway for us
using the lights from the patrol cars!

01:37:08.900 --> 01:37:11.110
That's my Kid-sama for you!

01:37:11.110 --> 01:37:12.780
I knew it all along!

01:37:14.070 --> 01:37:16.830
Ran, turn left once more.

01:37:17.490 --> 01:37:18.410
Got it.

01:37:36.470 --> 01:37:37.140
Kid!

01:37:37.140 --> 01:37:38.180
Find Kid!

01:37:38.470 --> 01:37:40.270
He has to be around here somewhere!

01:37:40.270 --> 01:37:41.350
Look everywhere!

01:37:44.940 --> 01:37:45.980
Is he there?

01:37:45.980 --> 01:37:46.980
Negative!

01:37:46.980 --> 01:37:47.770
How about over there?

01:37:49.840 --> 01:37:52.260
I'll leave the rest to you, Great Detective.

01:37:54.010 --> 01:37:58.390
All passengers, this plane will now make an emergency landing.

01:37:58.390 --> 01:38:01.730
Please fasten your seat belts tightly and obey
all directions from the flight attendants.

01:38:02.750 --> 01:38:06.380
Please remove all pens, eyeglasses, and high heeled
shoes and place them in your seatback pocket.

01:38:06.670 --> 01:38:09.840
Lean forward, and place your head in between your legs.

01:38:12.840 --> 01:38:13.510
Hey there, Ran.

01:38:14.090 --> 01:38:15.300
At last, it's time to land.

01:38:15.930 --> 01:38:17.220
What's the altitude and speed now?

01:38:17.720 --> 01:38:21.430
Height: 700 feet, 140 knots.

01:38:21.660 --> 01:38:25.040
All right, just keep maintaining a 3 degree descent.

01:38:25.040 --> 01:38:25.540
Sonoko!

01:38:26.210 --> 01:38:28.630
Pull down the gear lever and pull the flap lever!

01:38:29.270 --> 01:38:30.520
Gear lever?

01:38:30.520 --> 01:38:31.530
Flap?

01:38:31.780 --> 01:38:33.190
The gear lever is that one.

01:38:33.190 --> 01:38:34.240
And the flap is over there.

01:38:34.530 --> 01:38:35.240
Got it.

01:38:35.450 --> 01:38:37.240
Pull down the gear lever ...

01:38:37.620 --> 01:38:39.200
And pull the flap ...

01:38:41.910 --> 01:38:42.560
What?

01:38:42.600 --> 01:38:43.270
What happened?

01:38:43.950 --> 01:38:46.960
Shinichi, looks like we're out of fuel.

01:38:47.370 --> 01:38:48.540
Got it.

01:38:48.540 --> 01:38:50.090
There won't be any second chances ...

01:38:50.090 --> 01:38:51.170
It's one shot, do or die!

01:39:07.690 --> 01:39:09.230
Inspector Megure.

01:39:10.360 --> 01:39:12.400
It seems that plane ...

01:39:12.400 --> 01:39:14.110
It looks like it's flying this way, doesn't it?

01:39:15.650 --> 01:39:16.320
Why?

01:39:16.550 --> 01:39:17.470
Fifty.

01:39:17.950 --> 01:39:20.450
Raise the nose, and pull the thrust lever all the way up!

01:39:25.390 --> 01:39:26.180
Thirty.

01:39:27.520 --> 01:39:28.270
Twenty.

01:39:28.420 --> 01:39:29.750
All personnel evacuate!

01:39:30.400 --> 01:39:31.190
Ten.

01:39:34.630 --> 01:39:35.590
Bring the nose down!

01:39:38.840 --> 01:39:39.970
Reverse thrust!

01:39:52.460 --> 01:39:53.130
Stop!

01:39:53.130 --> 01:39:54.050
Stop, stop!

01:39:54.170 --> 01:39:54.840
Stop!

01:39:54.840 --> 01:39:56.010
Stop, stop!

01:40:00.070 --> 01:40:01.660
Shinichi, there's a crane!

01:40:01.820 --> 01:40:03.120
We're going to crash!

01:40:03.350 --> 01:40:03.930
Damn!

01:40:04.120 --> 01:40:04.790
The rudder!

01:40:04.790 --> 01:40:06.330
Use your right foot to press the rudder!

01:40:30.640 --> 01:40:31.560
It stopped!

01:40:32.020 --> 01:40:33.150
We stopped!

01:40:33.150 --> 01:40:34.020
All right!

01:40:40.590 --> 01:40:41.890
Kudou-kun ...

01:40:42.550 --> 01:40:45.010
I guess it wasn't in your dictionary either, huh?

01:40:46.220 --> 01:40:47.640
The word "impossible" ...

01:40:49.120 --> 01:40:50.910
You did it, Ran-neechan!

01:40:54.000 --> 01:40:54.920
Ran-neechan?

01:40:56.000 --> 01:40:56.750
Ran!

01:40:57.170 --> 01:40:57.760
Ran!

01:40:57.760 --> 01:40:58.840
Hang in there!

01:41:00.420 --> 01:41:01.470
Sonoko?

01:41:04.490 --> 01:41:06.620
They both just passed out ...

01:41:07.870 --> 01:41:08.700
Well, it was inevitable ...

01:41:09.500 --> 01:41:11.580
Since I ended up having you guys take on a monumental task.

01:41:14.840 --> 01:41:16.960
Good job, Ran.

01:41:17.750 --> 01:41:24.970
EYES, if you merely blink you may forget the sight

01:41:17.750 --> 01:41:24.970
Eyes mabataki sae wasuresou datta

01:41:26.010 --> 01:41:33.020
Of my smiling face as I casually pass you by

01:41:26.010 --> 01:41:33.020
madjika ni mita nanigenai watashi dake no egao

01:41:33.350 --> 01:41:47.740
The glittering light within your eyes is reflecting me with all your heart

01:41:33.350 --> 01:41:47.740
watashi wo utsushite ichizu ni hikaru kimi no hitomi no kagayaki ni michibikare

01:41:47.740 --> 01:41:53.750
And my path toward the future is changing

01:41:47.740 --> 01:41:53.750
mirai wa kawatteku

01:41:57.210 --> 01:42:06.220
From this moment on my heart pounds with this brilliance

01:41:57.210 --> 01:42:06.220
kore kara saki konna kirameku konna mune ga takanaru

01:42:06.550 --> 01:42:14.060
How many times do you suppose I can feel that way?

01:42:06.550 --> 01:42:14.060
omoi wo ikutsu kanjite iku to omou?

01:42:14.480 --> 01:42:21.690
Somehow, it's a little bit wonderful, somehow, I'm so happy

01:42:14.480 --> 01:42:21.690
nanka chotto tanoshii nanka sugoku ureshii

01:42:21.690 --> 01:42:29.700
Because with you, I am complete, DREAM x DREAM

01:42:21.690 --> 01:42:29.700
kimi to kansei shiteku Dream x Dream

01:42:30.240 --> 01:42:37.040
LIFE, when I am beside you, just like that

01:42:30.240 --> 01:42:37.040
Life tonari de kimi ooki na akubi

01:42:38.130 --> 01:42:44.630
I can't help but yawn when you do

01:42:38.130 --> 01:42:44.630
watashi ni mo utsutte nee sonna fuu na

01:42:44.970 --> 01:42:57.150
Even the tiniest bit of happiness is so precious when it comes to you

01:42:44.970 --> 01:42:57.150
chiisa na chiisa na shiawase ga totemo tokubetsu ni tonatte ikunda

01:42:57.150 --> 01:43:03.900
And without you, somehow, I wouldn't have it at all

01:42:57.150 --> 01:43:03.900
nante nai koto ga kimi to nara

01:43:04.110 --> 01:43:13.950
From this moment on, together we will shout out in joy of

01:43:04.110 --> 01:43:13.950
kore kara saki kimi to futari de hitotsu ni naru yorokobi wo

01:43:13.950 --> 01:43:20.630
Our happiness as the two of us become as one

01:43:13.950 --> 01:43:20.630
"shiawase" tte yonde iku koto ni naru

01:43:21.380 --> 01:43:28.800
Somehow, it's a little bit wonderful, somehow, I'm so happy

01:43:21.380 --> 01:43:28.800
nanka chotto tanoshii nanka sugoku ureshii

01:43:28.800 --> 01:43:36.310
Because with you, I am complete, DREAM x DREAM

01:43:28.800 --> 01:43:36.310
kimi to kansei shiteku Dream x Dream

01:43:45.780 --> 01:43:52.780
For how many seasons will you and I go in search of

